ABLE 1 — ERROR ROWS. One row per DISTINCT rejection/error branch. Format as a single pipe-delimited line:\n  function_name | exact trigger condition (the precise invalid input) | expected C result (exact return value: -1, NULL, abort)\nBe EXHAUSTIVE. Specifically make sure you cover:\n- crypto_sign_open / crypto_sign_verify_detached / _ed25519_open: signature S not canonical (sc25519_is_canonical fails), A has small order, ge25519_has_small_order(sig), ge25519_is_canonical(pk) fail, ge25519_frombytes fail, final crypto_verify_32 mismatch, smlen < 64 / smlen - 64 overflow, and the `#ifdef ED25519_COMPAT` vs default branch differences.\n- crypto_sign_ed25519_sk_to_* , _pk_to_curve25519 (non-canonical / small-order pk -> -1).\n- crypto_sign_init/update/final_create/final_verify (multi-part ph API).\n- crypto_scalarmult_curve25519: all-zero output check (`sodium_is_zero`), scalarmult_base, has_small_order n check in _ref10.\n- crypto_scalarmult_ed25519 / _noclamp / _base / _base_noclamp: zero scalar, non-canonical point, small order point, resulting identity.\n- crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255 / _base: zero scalar, invalid encoding.\n- crypto_core_ed25519_is_valid_point / _add / _sub / _from_uniform / _from_hash / _random / scalar ops (_scalar_invert with zero, _scalar_reduce, _scalar_negate/complement/add/sub/mul), crypto_core_ed25519_NONREDUCEDSCALARBYTES.\n- crypto_core_ristretto255_is_valid_point / _add / _sub / _from_hash / scalar ops.\n- crypto_generichash: outlen < crypto_generichash_BYTES_MIN(16) or > MAX(64), keylen bounds (0 or KEYBYTES_MIN 16..MAX 64), blake2b_init_key with keylen 0, blake2b_init_salt_personal, _init/_update/_final state, final outlen must match init outlen, crypto_generichash_statebytes.\n- crypto_hash_sha256/sha512 _init/_update/_final; sha3 variants; xof shake/turboshake (outlen 0? turboshake domain-separation byte range check e.g. must be 0x01..0x7f).\n- crypto_stream_*: mlen/clen bounds, ic (initial counter) variants _xor_ic, salsa20 _xor_ic u64 ic vs chacha20_ietf u32 ic overflow check, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX.\n- crypto_verify_16/32/64.\n- Any `_pick_best_implementation` / `crypto_*_primitive` dispatch returning NULL for unknown name.\n\nDELIVERABLE 2 — CONFIG AXES / SHAPES. Enumerate VALID-input axes the code branches on:\n- generichash: outlen at MIN/32/MAX, keylen 0/16/32/64, one-shot vs init/update/final, update chunking that crosses the 128-byte blake2b block (0,1,127,128,129,255,256 bytes), salt+personal variant.\n- sha256/sha512/sha3: message lengths 0,1,55,56,63,64,111,112,127,128,>1 block, multi-update chunking, padding boundaries.\n- xof shake128/256 + turboshake128/256: outlen < rate, == rate, > rate (multi-squeeze), absorb chunking, turboshake domain byte values.\n- stream ciphers: chacha20 (ref) vs chacha20_ietf; salsa20/2012/208; xsalsa20/xchacha20; mlen 0,1,63,64,65,block multiples, 512+ (multi-block loop), _xor_ic with ic 0 / 1 / near-2^32 / near-2^64.\n- ed25519/ristretto255 core: valid points, identity, small-order points, scalars 0/1/L-1/L/L+1/2^256-1, canonical vs non-canonical encodings, from_uniform/from_hash with random inputs.\n- sign: message len 0,1,64,>64; ed25519ph multi-part; sk_to_seed/sk_to_pk; keypair vs seed_keypair.\n- scalarmult: curve25519 base/point, ed25519 clamp vs noclamp, ristretto255.\nName each CONSTANT with its numeric value.\n\nOutput ONLY the two deliverables as plain text lines. Do not write any files."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":38965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":471,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"f79213df-9744-4865-ac26-a177bafc7c63","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:24:32.570Z"}
