n at MIN/32/MAX, keylen 0/16/32/64, one-shot vs init/update/final, update chunking that crosses the 128-byte blake2b block (0,1,127,128,129,255,256 bytes), salt+personal variant.\n- sha256/sha512/sha3: message lengths 0,1,55,56,63,64,111,112,127,128,>1 block, multi-update chunking, padding boundaries.\n- xof shake128/256 + turboshake128/256: outlen < rate, == rate, > rate (multi-squeeze), absorb chunking, turboshake domain byte values.\n- stream ciphers: chacha20 (ref) vs chacha20_ietf; salsa20/2012/208; xsalsa20/xchacha20; mlen 0,1,63,64,65,block multiples, 512+ (multi-block loop), _xor_ic with ic 0 / 1 / near-2^32 / near-2^64.\n- ed25519/ristretto255 core: valid points, identity, small-order points, scalars 0/1/L-1/L/L+1/2^256-1, canonical vs non-canonical encodings, from_uniform/from_hash with random inputs.\n- sign: message len 0,1,64,>64; ed25519ph multi-part; sk_to_seed/sk_to_pk; keypair vs seed_keypair.\n- scalarmult: curve25519 base/point, ed25519 clamp vs noclamp, ristretto255.\nName each CONSTANT with its numeric value.\n\nOutput ONLY the two deliverables as plain text lines. Do not write any files."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MEvboPLcASm417Fi9ey46g","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"755066a0-3b72-4b37-a309-36291172c1a9","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:24:32.572Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Enumerate sign/scalarmult/core errors"}
