th ===\ncrypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_verify / crypto_onetimeauth_verify | crypto_verify_16(h, correct) != 0 | returns -1\ncrypto_onetimeauth_poly1305 / _init / _update / _final (and crypto_onetimeauth* wrappers) | (no rejection branches; always return 0) | returns 0\npoly1305_update (donna & sse2) | (no error branch; only leftover-buffer bookkeeping) | void\n\n=== NULL-able unsigned long long *outlen POINTERS (all guarded by `if (p != NULL)`) ===\nclen_p: crypto_aead_{chacha20poly1305,chacha20poly1305_ietf,xchacha20poly1305_ietf,aegis128l,aegis256,aes256gcm}_encrypt, crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_afternm\nmaclen_p: crypto_aead_{chacha20poly1305,chacha20poly1305_ietf,xchacha20poly1305_ietf,aegis128l,aegis256,aes256gcm}_encrypt_detached, crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_detached_afternm\nmlen_p: crypto_aead_{chacha20poly1305,chacha20poly1305_ietf,xchacha20poly1305_ietf,aegis128l,aegis256,aes256gcm}_decrypt, crypto_aead_aes256gcm_decrypt_afternm\noutlen_p: crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_push\nmlen_p, tag_p: crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_pull (both individually NULL-able)\n\n=== NULL-able output-plaintext POINTERS (verify-only mode, distinct code path) ===\nm == NULL: crypto_aead_{chacha20poly1305,chacha20poly1305_ietf,xchacha20poly1305_ietf}_decrypt_detached (returns crypto_verify_16 result directly), crypto_aead_aes256gcm_decrypt_detached_afternm (routes to crypto_aead_aes256gcm_verify_mac), aegis128l/aegis256 decrypt_detached (decrypts into scratch `dst`), crypto_secretbox_open_detached, crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_open_detached (both return 0 after verify, no plaintext written)\nnsec: unused/(void)-cast in every AEAD (all *_NSECBYTES == 0U)\nad == NULL is legal only with adlen == 0 (poly1305/absorb loops never dereference); headers do not mark ad nonnull\n\n=== assert()/COMPILER_ASSERT (compile-time only; no runtime assert() anywhere in this area) ===\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK % 64U == 0U) - aead_chacha20poly1305.c, aead_xchacha20poly1305.c, crypto_secretbox_easy.c\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(sizeof computed_mac == 16U) - chacha/xchacha decrypt_detached\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(sizeof computed_mac >= 32) - aegis128l_common.h, aegis256_common.h\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(crypto_secretstream_..._MESSAGEBYTES_MAX <= crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX) - secretstream push\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(HEADERBYTES == hchacha20_INPUTBYTES + INONCEBYTES), (HEADERBYTES == xchacha20poly1305_ietf_NPUBBYTES), (sizeof state->nonce == INONCEBYTES + COUNTERBYTES), (poly1305_BYTES >= INONCEBYTES) - secretstream\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(64U >= ZEROBYTES), (ZEROBYTES >= poly1305_KEYBYTES) - secretbox_easy.c / secretbox_xchacha20poly1305.c\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(crypto_box_BEFORENMBYTES >= crypto_secretbox_KEYBYTES) - crypto_box_easy.c\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(crypto_box_PUBLICKEYBYTES < crypto_box_SEALBYTES) - crypto_box_seal.c and xchacha seal\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(sizeof *st_ >= sizeof *st) - aes256gcm beforenm\nCOMPILER_ASSERT(sizeof(crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_state) >= sizeof(poly1305_state_internal_t)) - poly1305_donna.c\n```\n\n## DELIVERABLE 2 — CONFIG AXES / SHAPES\n\n```\n=== GLOBAL ===\n- SODIUM_SIZE_MAX = SODIUM_MIN(UINT64_MAX, SIZE_MAX) = 2^64-1 on LP64. All *_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX derive from it.\n- sodium_misuse() runs an optional user handler then abort() (sodium/core.c:192); it never returns.\n- Runtime impl selection: _crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation, _crypto_aead_aegis256_pick_best_implementation, _crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_pick_best_implementation. With no HAVE_* macros, the pure-C fallbacks (aegis*_soft_implementation, crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_donna_implementation) are selected; they are also the static initializers, so they are active even before sodium_init().\n\n=== crypto_aead_aegis128l (KEYBYTES 16, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 16, ABYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-32, 2^61-1) = 2305843009213693951) ===\n- Entry points: _keybytes, _nsecbytes, _npubbytes, _abytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen, _encrypt, _decrypt, _encrypt_detached, _decrypt_detached (+ internal _crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation)\n- Implementation axis: aegis128l_soft.c is guarded by `#if 1` and is the default `implementation` -> the soft (softaes table) path is what runs when no HAVE_* macros are defined. Alternatives: aegis128l_aesni.c (HAVE_AVXINTRIN_H && HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H && runtime aesni&avx), aegis128l_armcrypto.c (HAVE_ARMCRYPTO && NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN && runtime armcrypto). All three share aegis128l_common.h so the shapes are identical.\n- RATE = 32 (aegis128l_common.h:1); AES_BLOCK_LENGTH = 16; state is 8 blocks; init runs 10 aegis128l_update rounds; mac runs 7 finalization rounds.\n- ad-length shapes: adlen 0 (all loops skipped) / 0<adlen<32 (partial-only: zero-padded src) / adlen 32 (one aegis128l_absorb) / adlen 33..63 (absorb + partial) / adlen 64 (one aegis128l_absorb2, the 2*RATE fast path) / adlen 65..127 / adlen 128 (two absorb2) / adlen % 32 != 0 tail\n- m-length shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 31 / 32 (exactly RATE, one aegis128l_enc, no tail) / 33 (block+1, enc + partial via src/dst scratch) / 64 / multi-block. Decrypt tail uses aegis128l_declast with len = mlen % 32.\n- decrypt m==NULL axis: full separate loop that decrypts into scratch `dst` and skips the memset-on-failure.\n- mac length axis inside aegis128l_mac: maclen==32 (public API: ABYTES) vs maclen==16 (dead code reachable only internally) vs other -> error.\n- in-place: no memmove/overlap handling; c and m must not partially overlap (unlike secretbox).\n- _encrypt is a thin wrapper: mac is written to c+mlen, so ciphertext buffer must be mlen+32.\n\n=== crypto_aead_aegis256 (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 32, ABYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-32, 2^61-1)) ===\n- Entry points: identical set to aegis128l (_keybytes/_nsecbytes/_npubbytes/_abytes/_messagebytes_max/_keygen/_encrypt/_decrypt/_encrypt_detached/_decrypt_detached)\n- Implementation axis: aegis256_soft.c (`#if 1`, default) vs aegis256_aesni.c vs aegis256_armcrypto.c; all share aegis256_common.h.\n- RATE = 16 (aegis256_common.h:1); state is 6 blocks; init runs 4 iterations x 4 aegis256_update = 16 rounds; mac runs 7 rounds.\n- ad shapes: adlen 0 / 1..15 (partial) / 16 (one aegis256_absorb) / 17..31 / 32 (one aegis256_absorb2, the 2*RATE path) / 33+ / adlen % 16 tail\n- m shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 (exact RATE) / 17 (block+1) / 32 / multi-block; declast for mlen % 16.\n- Same m==NULL scratch-decrypt axis and maclen 16/32 axis as aegis128l.\n\n=== crypto_aead_aes256gcm (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 12, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-16, 16*(2^32-2)) = 68719476704) ===\n- Entry points: _keybytes, _nsecbytes, _npubbytes, _abytes, _statebytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen, _is_available, _beforenm, _encrypt, _encrypt_detached, _encrypt_afternm, _encrypt_detached_afternm, _decrypt, _decrypt_detached, _decrypt_afternm, _decrypt_detached_afternm\n- Build axis (major): (a) neither HAVE_ARMCRYPTO+NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN nor HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H+HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H -> aead_aes256gcm.c ENOSYS stubs, _is_available()==0; (b) HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H+HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H -> aesni/, _is_available() = pclmul & aesni & avx; (c) HAVE_ARMCRYPTO+NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN -> armcrypto/.\n- crypto_aead_aes256gcm_state is CRYPTO_ALIGN(16); _statebytes() rounds sizeof up to a multiple of 16.\n- Precomputation axis: _beforenm expands the key and precomputes PC_COUNT = 2*PARALLEL_BLOCKS = 14 powers of H; the *_afternm entry points reuse it, the non-afternm ones build a stack state per call and sodium_memzero it.\n- PARALLEL_BLOCKS = 7, ROUNDS = 14; the encrypt/decrypt generics stride PARALLEL_BLOCKS*16 = 112 bytes.\n- Length shapes: ad_len/m_len 0 / 1..15 (zero-padded pad[16] via gh_ad_blocks) / 16 (one GHASH block) / 17..111 / 112 (PARALLEL_BLOCKS*16, the parallel fast path) / 113 (block+1) / 224 / multi-parallel-block; `ad_len & ~15` vs `ad_len & 15` split; counter starts at 2 for data, 1 for the tag block.\n- m == NULL axis in _decrypt_detached_afternm: routes to the separate crypto_aead_aes256gcm_verify_mac (GHASH-only, no AES-CTR).\n- required_blocks() is the only length gate: rejects m_blocks >= 2^32-2 and near-SIZE_MAX inputs.\n\n=== crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305 — ORIGINAL/8-byte-nonce variant (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 8, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _keybytes, _nsecbytes, _npubbytes, _abytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen, _encrypt, _encrypt_detached, _decrypt, _decrypt_detached\n- Poly1305 layout axis: NO 16-byte zero padding of ad or ciphertext; adlen and mlen are appended as two STORE64_LE lengths interleaved (adlen right after ad, mlen right after ciphertext). This is the pre-IETF construction and differs structurally from the _ietf variant.\n- Streaming axis: STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072 (a multiple of 64); encrypt loops in <=128 KiB chunks advancing a 64-bit ic (ic += cl/64) starting at ic = 1. Decrypt does a single crypto_stream_chacha20_xor_ic call with ic = 1 (no chunking).\n- Shapes: mlen 0 (while loop never entered) / 1 / 63 / 64 (exact chacha block) / 65 / 131072 (exact chunk) / 131073 (chunk+1, exercises the ic carry) / multi-chunk; adlen 0 vs >0; ad == NULL with adlen 0.\n- in-place c == m supported implicitly by crypto_stream_chacha20_xor_ic; no overlap fixups.\n\n=== crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 12, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-16, 64*(2^32-1)) = 274877906880) ===\n- Entry points: _ietf_keybytes, _ietf_nsecbytes, _ietf_npubbytes, _ietf_abytes, _ietf_messagebytes_max, _ietf_keygen, _ietf_encrypt, _ietf_encrypt_detached, _ietf_decrypt, _ietf_decrypt_detached. Uppercase aliases crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_IETF_* exist for the constants only.\n- Poly1305 layout axis: RFC 8439 - ad, then _pad0 of ((0x10 - adlen) & 0xf) bytes, then ciphertext, then _pad0 of ((0x10 - mlen) & 0xf), then STORE64_LE(adlen), STORE64_LE(mlen). Pad length is 0 exactly when adlen/mlen % 16 == 0 -> adlen/mlen 0, 16, 32 are the pad-free cases; 1 and 15 are the extremes of the padded case.\n- Streaming axis: same STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072, but ic is uint32_t (ic += (uint32_t)(cl/64)).\n- Shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 (pad-free) / 17 / 63 / 64 / 65 / 131072 / 131073 / multi-chunk; adlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 / 17.\n\n=== crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 24, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _ietf_keybytes, _ietf_nsecbytes, _ietf_npubbytes, _ietf_abytes, _ietf_messagebytes_max, _ietf_keygen, _ietf_encrypt, _ietf_encrypt_detached, _ietf_decrypt, _ietf_decrypt_detached (all funnel through static _encrypt_detached / _decrypt_detached). Uppercase _IETF_* constant aliases exist.\n- Nonce-derivation axis: crypto_core_hchacha20(k2, npub, k, NULL) over the first 16 bytes of npub; npub2 = 4 zero bytes || npub[16..23], so the inner call is a 12-byte-nonce ietf AEAD with an extended (chacha20_ietf_ext) counter.\n- Chunking axis (unique to this file): chunk = (mlen <= 64*(0xffffffff - 1)) ? STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK (131072) : mlen — messages above ~256 GiB are processed in a SINGLE pass because the 32-bit ietf_ext counter overflows into the IV and a chunk restart could not reproduce it. Boundary constant: 64*(2^32-2) = 274877906816.\n- Same RFC 8439 pad shapes as ietf (adlen/mlen 0/1/15/16/17), same mlen 0/1/63/64/65/131072/131073 boundaries.\n\n=== crypto_secretbox (PRIMITIVE \"xsalsa20poly1305\"; KEYBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, BOXZEROBYTES 16, ZEROBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: crypto_secretbox_keybytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _primitive, _keygen, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, plus deprecated _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, crypto_secretbox, crypto_secretbox_open\n- Primitive-level entry points: crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305{,_open}, _keybytes, _noncebytes, _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen\n- API-shape axis: easy/detached (MAC separate or prefixed, no padding) vs the deprecated NaCl API (requires 32 leading zero bytes in m, writes 16 leading zero bytes in c; mlen/clen must be >= 32)\n- Overlap axis (crypto_secretbox_detached and _open_detached only): explicit uintptr_t partial-overlap detection followed by memmove(c, m, mlen) / memmove(m, c, clen); so in-place, partially-overlapping-forward, partially-overlapping-backward, and fully disjoint are 4 distinct paths. crypto_secretbox_easy passes mac=c and c=c+16, which is exactly the overlapping case.\n- First-block axis: block0[64] holds ZEROBYTES(32) zeros followed by up to 64-32 = 32 message bytes; mlen0 = min(mlen, 32). So mlen 0 / 1 / 31 / 32 (mlen0 saturates, `mlen > mlen0` false) / 33 (first byte of the salsa20_xor_ic tail, ic = 1) / 64 / 131072 / 131073 are the interesting shapes.\n- Streaming axis: STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072 with 64-bit ic in _detached; _open_detached does a single crypto_stream_salsa20_xor_ic for clen > mlen0.\n- m == NULL axis in _open_detached: verify-only, returns 0 without writing plaintext.\n\n=== crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305 (KEYBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, private ZEROBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _keybytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max (no _keygen, no NaCl-style padded API, no _zerobytes/_boxzerobytes)\n- Same 4-way overlap/memmove axis and same mlen0 = min(mlen, 32) first-block axis as xsalsa20poly1305.\n- Difference from the xsalsa20 sibling: _detached calls crypto_stream_chacha20_xor over exactly mlen0+32 bytes (not a fixed 64) and then a single crypto_stream_chacha20_xor_ic(ic=1) for the whole tail; poly1305_update is called once over the full ciphertext (no 128 KiB chunking).\n- _open_detached always runs crypto_stream_chacha20_xor over a fixed 64 bytes for block0.\n\n=== crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305 (ABYTES 17 = 1 + xchacha20poly1305_ietf_ABYTES 16, HEADERBYTES 24 = xchacha20poly1305_ietf_NPUBBYTES, KEYBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-17, 64*(2^32-2)) = 274877906816) ===\n- Entry points: _statebytes, _abytes, _headerbytes, _keybytes, _messagebytes_max, _tag_message, _tag_push, _tag_rekey, _tag_final, _keygen, _init_push, _push, _init_pull, _pull, _rekey\n- TAG axis: TAG_MESSAGE 0x00, TAG_PUSH 0x01, TAG_REKEY 0x02, TAG_FINAL 0x03 (= TAG_PUSH|TAG_REKEY). Behavioural split is only on bit 0x02: TAG_REKEY and TAG_FINAL trigger an automatic crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_rekey; TAG_MESSAGE and TAG_PUSH do not. Arbitrary tag bytes (e.g. 0x42) are accepted and any with bit 0x02 set rekey.\n- State layout axis: state = { k[32] (chacha20_ietf key), nonce[12], _pad[8] }; nonce splits into COUNTERBYTES 4 (STATE_COUNTER, LE, reset to 1) + INONCEBYTES 8 (STATE_INONCE). Counter wrap to zero (sodium_is_zero) forces an implicit rekey — i.e. an automatic rekey every 2^32-1 messages.\n- Per-message chacha20_ietf counter blocks: 0 = poly1305 key block, 1 = the tag block, 2.. = payload. Payload therefore caps at 64*(2^32-2) bytes.\n- Explicit rekey axis: crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_rekey re-derives k||inonce (40 bytes) from itself with chacha20_ietf_xor and resets the counter; callable by the app at any point on either side, and both sides must call it symmetrically.\n- MAC-chaining axis: STATE_INONCE is XOR'd with the first 8 bytes of the poly1305 tag after every push/pull, so message ordering is part of the state.\n- Poly1305 layout axis: ad, _pad0 ((0x10 - adlen) & 0xf), the 64-byte encrypted tag block, ciphertext, then _pad0 of ((0x10 - 64 + mlen) & 0xf) — the source explicitly documents this as a bug (should have been (0x10 - (64 + mlen)) & 0xf), then STORE64_LE(adlen) and STORE64_LE(64 + mlen).\n- Shapes: adlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 / 17; mlen 0 (output is exactly 17 bytes) / 1 / 15 / 16 / 48 (makes (0x10 - 64 + mlen)&0xf == 0) / 63 / 64 / 65; inlen exactly 17 (empty message) vs 16 (rejected).\n- init_pull accepts any 24-byte header without validation; a wrong header is only detected as a MAC failure on the first _pull.\n\n=== crypto_box (PRIMITIVE \"curve25519xsalsa20poly1305\"; SEEDBYTES 32, PUBLICKEYBYTES 32, SECRETKEYBYTES 32, BEFORENMBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, BOXZEROBYTES 16, ZEROBYTES 32, SEALBYTES 48, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _seedbytes, _publickeybytes, _secretkeybytes, _beforenmbytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _primitive, _sealbytes, _seed_keypair, _keypair, _beforenm, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _easy_afternm, _open_easy_afternm, _detached_afternm, _open_detached_afternm, _afternm, _open_afternm, _seal, _seal_open, plus deprecated _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, crypto_box, crypto_box_open\n- Key-derivation axis: _keypair (randombytes_buf sk then scalarmult_base) vs _seed_keypair (sk = first 32 bytes of SHA-512(seed[32])) — deterministic vs random.\n- Precomputation axis: _beforenm(k, pk, sk) = hsalsa20(scalarmult(sk, pk), zero[16]) -> 32-byte shared key, reused by all *_afternm entry points; the non-afternm entry points derive it on the stack and sodium_memzero it.\n- API-shape axis: easy (MAC prepended, no padding) / detached (separate mac) / afternm (precomputed k) / seal (anonymous sender: 32-byte ephemeral pk prepended, nonce = BLAKE2b-24(epk || recipient_pk)) / deprecated NaCl padded (requires 32 leading zeros in m, 16 leading zeros in c)\n- crypto_box_detached_afternm and _open_detached_afternm are pure aliases of crypto_secretbox_detached / _open_detached, so they inherit the whole overlap-memmove and mlen0 = min(mlen,32) shape set.\n- Seal shapes: clen exactly 48 (empty sealed message) / 49 / >48; the c buffer must be mlen+48.\n\n=== crypto_box_curve25519xchacha20poly1305 (SEEDBYTES 32, PUBLICKEYBYTES 32, SECRETKEYBYTES 32, BEFORENMBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, SEALBYTES 48, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _seedbytes, _publickeybytes, _secretkeybytes, _beforenmbytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _sealbytes, _seed_keypair, _keypair, _beforenm, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _easy_afternm, _open_easy_afternm, _detached_afternm, _open_detached_afternm, _seal, _seal_open\n- No deprecated padded NaCl API and no plain _afternm/_open_afternm variants (unlike the xsalsa20 sibling) — the only afternm forms are the easy/detached ones.\n- _beforenm uses crypto_core_hchacha20 (not hsalsa20) over the scalarmult output; nonce for seal is BLAKE2b-24(epk || pk).\n- _detached_afternm / _open_detached_afternm are aliases of crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_detached / _open_detached, inheriting that file's overlap and mlen0 shapes.\n\n=== crypto_auth (PRIMITIVE \"hmacsha512256\"; BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32) ===\n- Entry points: crypto_auth_bytes, _keybytes, _primitive, crypto_auth, crypto_auth_verify, crypto_auth_keygen\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha512256: BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha512256, _verify. state is cast to crypto_auth_hmacsha512_state; _final truncates the 64-byte SHA-512 HMAC to 32 bytes.\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha512: BYTES 64, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha512, _verify. Block size 128.\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha256: BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha256, _verify. Block size 64.\n- Key-length axis in _init (the main config axis): keylen == 0 with key == NULL (legal, pads are unmodified 0x36/0x5c) / keylen 1..block_size with non-NULL key (direct XOR into pad) / keylen == block_size exactly (64 for sha256, 128 for sha512) / keylen > block_size (key is pre-hashed with the SAME state->ictx and replaced by khash, keylen set to 32 or 64) / key == NULL with keylen > 0 (misuse -> abort). The one-shot crypto_auth_hmacsha*() always passes keylen = KEYBYTES = 32.\n- Streaming axis: _init / _update (callable any number of times with any inlen, including 0) / _final; state holds two SHA-2 contexts (ictx, octx).\n- _verify combines crypto_verify_{32,64}(h, correct) | (-(h == correct)) | sodium_memcmp(correct, h, n) — the pointer-aliasing term is defensive (correct is a local, so it is always 0).\n\n=== crypto_onetimeauth (PRIMITIVE \"poly1305\"; BYTES 16, KEYBYTES 32) ===\n- Entry points: crypto_onetimeauth_statebytes, _bytes, _keybytes, _primitive, crypto_onetimeauth, crypto_onetimeauth_verify, _init, _update, _final, _keygen\n- Primitive-level: crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305, _verify, _init, _update, _final, _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, plus internal _crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_pick_best_implementation\n- Implementation axis: donna (poly1305_donna.c; the static default, so it is the one used when no HAVE_* macros are defined) vs sse2 (poly1305_sse2.c, only when HAVE_TI_MODE && HAVE_EMMINTRIN_H && runtime sse2). Within donna there is a further compile-time split: poly1305_donna64.h when HAVE_TI_MODE, else poly1305_donna32.h.\n- BLOCK-SIZE AXIS (differs per implementation): poly1305_block_size == 16 for donna, == 32 for sse2. The state's leftover buffer is that size, so the chunking boundaries that matter are implementation-dependent.\n- update/leftover axis in poly1305_update: (a) leftover == 0 and bytes < block_size -> pure buffering; (b) leftover != 0 and want > bytes -> top up the buffer only, leftover < block_size, early return; (c) leftover != 0 and the top-up exactly fills the buffer -> one poly1305_blocks on st->buffer, leftover = 0; (d) bytes >= block_size after that -> poly1305_blocks over bytes & ~(block_size-1); (e) a nonzero remainder is stored back as leftover. Interesting chunkings: 1+15, 15+1, 16 in one call, 16 in two calls, 17, 31+1, 32, 33, and (for sse2) 31/32/33.\n- finish axis: leftover == 0 (no final partial block) vs leftover in 1..block_size-1 (0x01 pad byte appended, rest zeroed); sse2 additionally branches on leftover == 16, leftover < 16, and leftover > 16 (poly1305_final_shift8 vs poly1305_final_shift16).\n- Callers in this area that drive the update chunking: every AEAD/secretbox/secretstream in this report calls _update with ad, then a 0..15-byte _pad0, then ciphertext, then a 0..15-byte _pad0, then two 8-byte length words — so a 0-length _update call and back-to-back sub-block _update calls are on the normal path.\n```\n\nEverything above is derived from the files under `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/{crypto_aead,crypto_secretbox,crypto_secretstream,crypto_box,crypto_auth,crypto_onetimeauth}` and the matching headers in `.../libsodium/include/sodium/`. No files were modified.\n\nThree findings worth flagging to the caller as likely translation traps:\n\n1. `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_afternm` (aesni line 208, armcrypto equivalent) sets `*clen_p = mlen + ABYTES` **without checking `ret`**, unlike `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt` which sets it to 0 on failure. A faithful port must reproduce this asymmetry.\n2. AEGIS `*_encrypt_detached` writes `*maclen_p` **before** the `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` check, so the out-param is already mutated on the abort path.\n3. `crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_push`/`_pull` use `(0x10 - (sizeof block) + mlen) & 0xf` for the ciphertext pad — the source comments this as a deviation from the intended `(0x10 - (sizeof block + mlen)) & 0xf`. It is wire-format-visible and must be preserved bit-for-bit.","usage":{"total_tokens":133287,"tool_uses":41,"duration_ms":377697},"uuid":"cb144e09-5a94-4cdd-8ae3-1726641fb35a","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051"}
