ZE_MAX-32, 2^61-1) = 2305843009213693951) ===\n- Entry points: _keybytes, _nsecbytes, _npubbytes, _abytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen, _encrypt, _decrypt, _encrypt_detached, _decrypt_detached (+ internal _crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation)\n- Implementation axis: aegis128l_soft.c is guarded by `#if 1` and is the default `implementation` -> the soft (softaes table) path is what runs when no HAVE_* macros are defined. Alternatives: aegis128l_aesni.c (HAVE_AVXINTRIN_H && HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H && runtime aesni&avx), aegis128l_armcrypto.c (HAVE_ARMCRYPTO && NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN && runtime armcrypto). All three share aegis128l_common.h so the shapes are identical.\n- RATE = 32 (aegis128l_common.h:1); AES_BLOCK_LENGTH = 16; state is 8 blocks; init runs 10 aegis128l_update rounds; mac runs 7 finalization rounds.\n- ad-length shapes: adlen 0 (all loops skipped) / 0<adlen<32 (partial-only: zero-padded src) / adlen 32 (one aegis128l_absorb) / adlen 33..63 (absorb + partial) / adlen 64 (one aegis128l_absorb2, the 2*RATE fast path) / adlen 65..127 / adlen 128 (two absorb2) / adlen % 32 != 0 tail\n- m-length shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 31 / 32 (exactly RATE, one aegis128l_enc, no tail) / 33 (block+1, enc + partial via src/dst scratch) / 64 / multi-block. Decrypt tail uses aegis128l_declast with len = mlen % 32.\n- decrypt m==NULL axis: full separate loop that decrypts into scratch `dst` and skips the memset-on-failure.\n- mac length axis inside aegis128l_mac: maclen==32 (public API: ABYTES) vs maclen==16 (dead code reachable only internally) vs other -> error.\n- in-place: no memmove/overlap handling; c and m must not partially overlap (unlike secretbox).\n- _encrypt is a thin wrapper: mac is written to c+mlen, so ciphertext buffer must be mlen+32.\n\n=== crypto_aead_aegis256 (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 32, ABYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-32, 2^61-1)) ===\n- Entry points: identical set to aegis128l (_keybytes/_nsecbytes/_npubbytes/_abytes/_messagebytes_max/_keygen/_encrypt/_decrypt/_encrypt_detached/_decrypt_detached)\n- Implementation axis: aegis256_soft.c (`#if 1`, default) vs aegis256_aesni.c vs aegis256_armcrypto.c; all share aegis256_common.h.\n- RATE = 16 (aegis256_common.h:1); state is 6 blocks; init runs 4 iterations x 4 aegis256_update = 16 rounds; mac runs 7 rounds.\n- ad shapes: adlen 0 / 1..15 (partial) / 16 (one aegis256_absorb) / 17..31 / 32 (one aegis256_absorb2, the 2*RATE path) / 33+ / adlen % 16 tail\n- m shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 (exact RATE) / 17 (block+1) / 32 / multi-block; declast for mlen % 16.\n- Same m==NULL scratch-decrypt axis and maclen 16/32 axis as aegis128l.\n\n=== crypto_aead_aes256gcm (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 12, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-16, 16*(2^32-2)) = 68719476704) ===\n- Entry points: _keybytes, _nsecbytes, _npubbytes, _abytes, _statebytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen, _is_available, _beforenm, _encrypt, _encrypt_detached, _encrypt_afternm, _encrypt_detached_afternm, _decrypt, _decrypt_detached, _decrypt_afternm, _decrypt_detached_afternm\n- Build axis (major): (a) neither HAVE_ARMCRYPTO+NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN nor HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H+HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H -> aead_aes256gcm.c ENOSYS stubs, _is_available()==0; (b) HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H+HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H -> aesni/, _is_available() = pclmul & aesni & avx; (c) HAVE_ARMCRYPTO+NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN -> armcrypto/.\n- crypto_aead_aes256gcm_state is CRYPTO_ALIGN(16); _statebytes() rounds sizeof up to a multiple of 16.\n- Precomputation axis: _beforenm expands the key and precomputes PC_COUNT = 2*PARALLEL_BLOCKS = 14 powers of H; the *_afternm entry points reuse it, the non-afternm ones build a stack state per call and sodium_memzero it.\n- PARALLEL_BLOCKS = 7, ROUNDS = 14; the encrypt/decrypt generics stride PARALLEL_BLOCKS*16 = 112 bytes.\n- Length shapes: ad_len/m_len 0 / 1..15 (zero-padded pad[16] via gh_ad_blocks) / 16 (one GHASH block) / 17..111 / 112 (PARALLEL_BLOCKS*16, the parallel fast path) / 113 (block+1) / 224 / mu