text, then _pad0 of ((0x10 - mlen) & 0xf), then STORE64_LE(adlen), STORE64_LE(mlen). Pad length is 0 exactly when adlen/mlen % 16 == 0 -> adlen/mlen 0, 16, 32 are the pad-free cases; 1 and 15 are the extremes of the padded case.\n- Streaming axis: same STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072, but ic is uint32_t (ic += (uint32_t)(cl/64)).\n- Shapes: mlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 (pad-free) / 17 / 63 / 64 / 65 / 131072 / 131073 / multi-chunk; adlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 / 17.\n\n=== crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf (KEYBYTES 32, NSECBYTES 0, NPUBBYTES 24, ABYTES 16, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _ietf_keybytes, _ietf_nsecbytes, _ietf_npubbytes, _ietf_abytes, _ietf_messagebytes_max, _ietf_keygen, _ietf_encrypt, _ietf_encrypt_detached, _ietf_decrypt, _ietf_decrypt_detached (all funnel through static _encrypt_detached / _decrypt_detached). Uppercase _IETF_* constant aliases exist.\n- Nonce-derivation axis: crypto_core_hchacha20(k2, npub, k, NULL) over the first 16 bytes of npub; npub2 = 4 zero bytes || npub[16..23], so the inner call is a 12-byte-nonce ietf AEAD with an extended (chacha20_ietf_ext) counter.\n- Chunking axis (unique to this file): chunk = (mlen <= 64*(0xffffffff - 1)) ? STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK (131072) : mlen — messages above ~256 GiB are processed in a SINGLE pass because the 32-bit ietf_ext counter overflows into the IV and a chunk restart could not reproduce it. Boundary constant: 64*(2^32-2) = 274877906816.\n- Same RFC 8439 pad shapes as ietf (adlen/mlen 0/1/15/16/17), same mlen 0/1/63/64/65/131072/131073 boundaries.\n\n=== crypto_secretbox (PRIMITIVE \"xsalsa20poly1305\"; KEYBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, BOXZEROBYTES 16, ZEROBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: crypto_secretbox_keybytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _primitive, _keygen, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, plus deprecated _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, crypto_secretbox, crypto_secretbox_open\n- Primitive-level entry points: crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305{,_open}, _keybytes, _noncebytes, _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _keygen\n- API-shape axis: easy/detached (MAC separate or prefixed, no padding) vs the deprecated NaCl API (requires 32 leading zero bytes in m, writes 16 leading zero bytes in c; mlen/clen must be >= 32)\n- Overlap axis (crypto_secretbox_detached and _open_detached only): explicit uintptr_t partial-overlap detection followed by memmove(c, m, mlen) / memmove(m, c, clen); so in-place, partially-overlapping-forward, partially-overlapping-backward, and fully disjoint are 4 distinct paths. crypto_secretbox_easy passes mac=c and c=c+16, which is exactly the overlapping case.\n- First-block axis: block0[64] holds ZEROBYTES(32) zeros followed by up to 64-32 = 32 message bytes; mlen0 = min(mlen, 32). So mlen 0 / 1 / 31 / 32 (mlen0 saturates, `mlen > mlen0` false) / 33 (first byte of the salsa20_xor_ic tail, ic = 1) / 64 / 131072 / 131073 are the interesting shapes.\n- Streaming axis: STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK = 131072 with 64-bit ic in _detached; _open_detached does a single crypto_stream_salsa20_xor_ic for clen > mlen0.\n- m == NULL axis in _open_detached: verify-only, returns 0 without writing plaintext.\n\n=== crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305 (KEYBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, private ZEROBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _keybytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max (no _keygen, no NaCl-style padded API, no _zerobytes/_boxzerobytes)\n- Same 4-way overlap/memmove axis and same mlen0 = min(mlen, 32) first-block axis as xsalsa20poly1305.\n- Difference from the xsalsa20 sibling: _detached calls crypto_stream_chacha20_xor over exactly mlen0+32 bytes (not a fixed 64) and then a single crypto_stream_chacha20_xor_ic(ic=1) for the whole tail; poly1305_update is called once over the full ciphertext (no 128 KiB chunking).\n- _open_detached always runs crypto_stream_chacha20_xor over a fixed 64 bytes for block0.\n\n=== crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305 (ABYTES 17 = 1 + xchacha20poly1305_ietf_ABYTES 16, HEADERBYTES 24 = xchacha20poly1305_ietf_NPUBBYTES, KEYBYTES 32, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = min(SIZE_MAX-17, 64*(2^32-2)) = 274877906816) ===\n- Entry points: _statebytes, _abytes, _headerbytes, _keybytes, _messagebytes_max, _tag_message, _tag_push, _tag_rekey, _tag_final, _keygen, _init_push, _push, _init_pull, _pull, _rekey\n- TAG axis: TAG_MESSAGE 0x00, TAG_PUSH 0x01, TAG_REKEY 0x02, TAG_FINAL 0x03 (= TAG_PUSH|TAG_REKEY). Behavioural split is only on bit 0x02: TAG_REKEY and TAG_FINAL trigger an automatic crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_rekey; TAG_MESSAGE and TAG_PUSH do not. Arbitrary tag bytes (e.g. 0x42) are accepted and any with bit 0x02 set rekey.\n- State layout axis: state = { k[32] (chacha20_ietf key), nonce[12], _pad[8] }; nonce splits into COUNTERBYTES 4 (STATE_COUNTER, LE, reset to 1) + INONCEBYTES 8 (STATE_INONCE). Counter wrap to zero (sodium_is_zero) forces an implicit rekey — i.e. an automatic rekey every 2^32-1 messages.\n- Per-message chacha20_ietf counter blocks: 0 = poly1305 key block, 1 = the tag block, 2.. = payload. Payload therefore caps at 64*(2^32-2) bytes.\n- Explicit rekey axis: crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_rekey re-derives k||inonce (40 bytes) from itself with chacha20_ietf_xor and resets the counter; callable by the app at any point on either side, and both sides must call it symmetrically.\n- MAC-chaining axis: STATE_INONCE is XOR'd with the first 8 bytes of the poly1305 tag after every push/pull, so message ordering is part of the state.\n- Poly1305 layout axis: ad, _pad0 ((0x10 - adlen) & 0xf), the 64-byte encrypted tag block, ciphertext, then _pad0 of ((0x10 - 64 + mlen) & 0xf) — the source explicitly documents this as a bug (should have been (0x10 - (64 + mlen)) & 0xf), then STORE64_LE(adlen) and STORE64_LE(64 + mlen).\n- Shapes: adlen 0 / 1 / 15 / 16 / 17; mlen 0 (output is exactly 17 bytes) / 1 / 15 / 16 / 48 (makes (0x10 - 64 + mlen)&0xf == 0) / 63 / 64 / 65; inlen exactly 17 (empty message) vs 16 (rejected).\n- init_pull accepts any 24-byte header without validation; a wrong header is only detected as a MAC failure on the first _pull.\n\n=== crypto_box (PRIMITIVE \"curve25519xsalsa20poly1305\"; SEEDBYTES 32, PUBLICKEYBYTES 32, SECRETKEYBYTES 32, BEFORENMBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, BOXZEROBYTES 16, ZEROBYTES 32, SEALBYTES 48, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _seedbytes, _publickeybytes, _secretkeybytes, _beforenmbytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _primitive, _sealbytes, _seed_keypair, _keypair, _beforenm, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _easy_afternm, _open_easy_afternm, _detached_afternm, _open_detached_afternm, _afternm, _open_afternm, _seal, _seal_open, plus deprecated _zerobytes, _boxzerobytes, crypto_box, crypto_box_open\n- Key-derivation axis: _keypair (randombytes_buf sk then scalarmult_base) vs _seed_keypair (sk = first 32 bytes of SHA-512(seed[32])) — deterministic vs random.\n- Precomputation axis: _beforenm(k, pk, sk) = hsalsa20(scalarmult(sk, pk), zero[16]) -> 32-byte shared key, reused by all *_afternm entry points; the non-afternm entry points derive it on the stack and sodium_memzero it.\n- API-shape axis: easy (MAC prepended, no padding) / detached (separate mac) / afternm (precomputed k) / seal (anonymous sender: 32-byte ephemeral pk prepended, nonce = BLAKE2b-24(epk || recipient_pk)) / deprecated NaCl padded (requires 32 leading zeros in m, 16 leading zeros in c)\n- crypto_box_detached_afternm and _open_detached_afternm are pure aliases of crypto_secretbox_detached / _open_detached, so they inherit the whole overlap-memmove and mlen0 = min(mlen,32) shape set.\n- Seal shapes: clen exactly 48 (empty sealed message) / 49 / >48; the c buffer must be mlen+48.\n\n=== crypto_box_curve25519xchacha20poly1305 (SEEDBYTES 32, PUBLICKEYBYTES 32, SECRETKEYBYTES 32, BEFORENMBYTES 32, NONCEBYTES 24, MACBYTES 16, SEALBYTES 48, MESSAGEBYTES_MAX = SODIUM_SIZE_MAX-16) ===\n- Entry points: _seedbytes, _publickeybytes, _secretkeybytes, _beforenmbytes, _noncebytes, _macbytes, _messagebytes_max, _sealbytes, _seed_keypair, _keypair, _beforenm, _easy, _open_easy, _detached, _open_detached, _easy_afternm, _open_easy_afternm, _detached_afternm, _open_detached_afternm, _seal, _seal_open\n- No deprecated padded NaCl API and no plain _afternm/_open_afternm variants (unlike the xsalsa20 sibling) — the only afternm forms are the easy/detached ones.\n- _beforenm uses crypto_core_hchacha20 (not hsalsa20) over the scalarmult output; nonce for seal is BLAKE2b-24(epk || pk).\n- _detached_afternm / _open_detached_afternm are aliases of crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_detached / _open_detached, inheriting that file's overlap and mlen0 shapes.\n\n=== crypto_auth (PRIMITIVE \"hmacsha512256\"; BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32) ===\n- Entry points: crypto_auth_bytes, _keybytes, _primitive, crypto_auth, crypto_auth_verify, crypto_auth_keygen\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha512256: BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha512256, _verify. state is cast to crypto_auth_hmacsha512_state; _final truncates the 64-byte SHA-512 HMAC to 32 bytes.\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha512: BYTES 64, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha512, _verify. Block size 128.\n- crypto_auth_hmacsha256: BYTES 32, KEYBYTES 32 — _bytes, _keybytes, _statebytes, _keygen, _init, _update, _final, crypto_auth_hmacsha256, _verify. Block size 64.\n- Key-length axis in _init (the main config axis): keylen == 0 with key == NULL (legal, pads are unmodified 0x36/0x5c) / keylen 1..block_size with non-NULL key (direct XOR into pad) / keylen == block_size exactly (64 for sha256, 128 for sha512) / keylen > block_size (key is pre-hashed with the SAME state->ictx and replaced by khash, keylen set to 32 or 64