xis: leftover == 0 (no final partial block) vs leftover in 1..block_size-1 (0x01 pad byte appended, rest zeroed); sse2 additionally branches on leftover == 16, leftover < 16, and leftover > 16 (poly1305_final_shift8 vs poly1305_final_shift16).\n- Callers in this area that drive the update chunking: every AEAD/secretbox/secretstream in this report calls _update with ad, then a 0..15-byte _pad0, then ciphertext, then a 0..15-byte _pad0, then two 8-byte length words — so a 0-length _update call and back-to-back sub-block _update calls are on the normal path.\n```\n\nEverything above is derived from the files under `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/{crypto_aead,crypto_secretbox,crypto_secretstream,crypto_box,crypto_auth,crypto_onetimeauth}` and the matching headers in `.../libsodium/include/sodium/`. No files were modified.\n\nThree findings worth flagging to the caller as likely translation traps:\n\n1. `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt_afternm` (aesni line 208, armcrypto equivalent) sets `*clen_p = mlen + ABYTES` **without checking `ret`**, unlike `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_encrypt` which sets it to 0 on failure. A faithful port must reproduce this asymmetry.\n2. AEGIS `*_encrypt_detached` writes `*maclen_p` **before** the `MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` check, so the out-param is already mutated on the abort path.\n3. `crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_push`/`_pull` use `(0x10 - (sizeof block) + mlen) & 0xf` for the ciphertext pad — the source comments this as a deviation from the intended `(0x10 - (sizeof block + mlen)) & 0xf`. It is wire-format-visible and must be preserved bit-for-bit."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":377700,"totalTokens":158868,"totalToolUseCount":41,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2031,"cache_read_input_tokens":130801,"output_tokens":26034,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5951},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_req