TRPREFIX = \"$argon2id$\"; crypto_pwhash_STRPREFIX = \"$argon2id$\"\n\nPWHASH ARGON2 — opslimit (t_cost) axis\nargon2i | OPSLIMIT_MIN=3, OPSLIMIT_INTERACTIVE=4, OPSLIMIT_MODERATE=6, OPSLIMIT_SENSITIVE=8, OPSLIMIT_MAX=4294967295\nargon2id | OPSLIMIT_MIN=1, OPSLIMIT_INTERACTIVE=2, OPSLIMIT_MODERATE=3, OPSLIMIT_SENSITIVE=4, OPSLIMIT_MAX=4294967295\nargon2 core | passes = t_cost, loop `for (pass=0; pass<passes; pass++)` — t_cost=1 (single pass, argon2id fully data-dependent only in slices 2,3) vs t_cost=3 (multi-pass, argon2id data-dependent everywhere from pass 1 on); ARGON2_MIN_TIME=1, ARGON2_MAX_TIME=4294967295\n\nPWHASH ARGON2 — memlimit (m_cost) axis\nargon2i / argon2id | MEMLIMIT_MIN=8192 bytes (=8 KiB → m_cost=8 blocks = ARGON2_MIN_MEMORY), MEMLIMIT_INTERACTIVE=33554432 (argon2i) / 67108864 (argon2id), MEMLIMIT_MODERATE=134217728 (argon2i) / 268435456 (argon2id), MEMLIMIT_SENSITIVE=536870912 (argon2i) / 1073741824 (argon2id), MEMLIMIT_MAX=4398046510080 on 64-bit (2147483648 if SIZE_MAX>=2^31, else 32768)\nargon2 core | m_cost is memlimit/1024; ARGON2_MIN_MEMORY = 2*ARGON2_SYNC_POINTS = 8; ARGON2_MAX_MEMORY = min(0xFFFFFFFF, 1<<ARGON2_MAX_MEMORY_BITS) = 4294967295 on 64-bit (ARGON2_MAX_MEMORY_BITS = min(32, sizeof(void*)*CHAR_BIT-11) = 32)\nargon2 core | m_cost is rounded: memory_blocks = max(m_cost, 2*4*lanes); segment_length = memory_blocks/(lanes*4); memory_blocks = segment_length*lanes*4 — so m_cost values not divisible by 4*lanes are silently rounded DOWN (shape: m_cost=8 vs 9 vs 12 give same/different block counts)\n\nPWHASH ARGON2 — lanes/threads axis\nlibsodium public API | always passes parallelism = 1 for both lanes and threads (pwhash_argon2i.c:172, pwhash_argon2id.c:168) — the multi-lane path is reachable only via argon2_hash/argon2_ctx or via a decoded \"p=\" field\nargon2_ctx | ARGON2_MIN_LANES=1, ARGON2_MAX_LANES=16777215 (0xFFFFFF), ARGON2_MIN_THREADS=1, ARGON2_MAX_THREADS=16777215; ARGON2_SYNC_POINTS=4 slices per pass; lane_length = segment_length*4\nargon2 core | there is no threading: argon2_fill_memory_blocks loops slices s=0..3 then lanes l=0..lanes-1 serially, so `threads` only affects validation and the initial hash (context->lanes is hashed, threads is not)\nargon2 fill implementation | fill_segment default = argon2_fill_segment_ref (or argon2_fill_segment_neon on aarch64+NEON); _crypto_pwhash_argon2_pick_best_implementation() may select avx512f/avx2/ssse3/wasm32 — all bit-identical, ref-only for this port\n\nPWHASH ARGON2 — output length axis\ncrypto_pwhash_BYTES_MIN = crypto_pwhash_argon2id_BYTES_MIN = crypto_pwhash_argon2i_BYTES_MIN = 16 (== ARGON2_MIN_OUTLEN)\ncrypto_pwhash_BYTES_MAX = min(SODIUM_SIZE_MAX, 4294967295) = 4294967295 (== ARGON2_MAX_OUTLEN)\nblake2b_long shape | outlen <= crypto_generichash_blake2b_BYTES_MAX (=64): single init/update/update/final. outlen > 64: chunked mode — first 32 bytes, then loop while toproduce > 64 emitting 32 bytes/iteration, final short block of `toproduce` bytes. Test at outlen = 16, 32, 64, 65, 96, 128 to cover both arms and the loop.\nargon2 str hash length | STR_HASHBYTES = 32 (fixed for _str/_str_verify); ARGON2_BLOCK_SIZE=1024, ARGON2_PREHASH_DIGEST_LENGTH=64, ARGON2_PREHASH_SEED_LENGTH=72, ARGON2_QWORDS_IN_BLOCK=128, ARGON2_ADDRESSES_IN_BLOCK=128\n\nPWHASH ARGON2 — password / salt axes\ncrypto_pwhash_PASSWD_MIN = 0 (empty password is VALID), crypto_pwhash_PASSWD_MAX = 4294967295; shapes: passwdlen 0 (pwd may be non-NULL), 1, 16, >1024\ncrypto_pwhash_SALTBYTES = crypto_pwhash_argon2i_SALTBYTES = crypto_pwhash_argon2id_SALTBYTES = 16 (fixed; salt always exactly 16 bytes at the public API)\nargon2_ctx salt range | ARGON2_MIN_SALT_LENGTH=8, ARGON2_MAX_SALT_LENGTH=4294967295 (8..16..longer reachable only via argon2_hash / decoded strings)\noptional inputs (secret/ad) | ARGON2_MIN_SECRET=0/ARGON2_MAX_SECRET=4294967295, ARGON2_MIN_AD_LENGTH=0/ARGON2_MAX_AD_LENGTH=4294967295 — always NULL/0 from the libsodium API; flags axis ARGON2_DEFAULT_FLAGS=0 vs ARGON2_FLA