pto_kem_mlkem768_enc (random 32-byte m) vs crypto_kem_mlkem768_enc_deterministic (caller-supplied 32-byte seed) — deterministic KAT path; pk canonicality is validated\ndec axes | valid ct (fail_mask=0 → true shared secret) vs tampered ct (fail_mask=0xFF → implicit rejection k_bar = SHAKE256(z ‖ ct)) — both return 0; cmov is the constant-time selector\nrejection sampling axis | gen_matrix / rej_uniform refill loop: GEN_MATRIX_NBLOCKS blocks of crypto_xof_shake128_BLOCKBYTES; the `while (ctr < 256)` refill arm fires only for some seeds — seed-dependent extra-squeeze coverage; transposed=0 (keypair) vs transposed=1 (enc)\n\nKEM XWING\nconstants | crypto_kem_xwing_PUBLICKEYBYTES=1216 (=1184 ML-KEM ‖ 32 X25519), SECRETKEYBYTES=32 (the raw seed), CIPHERTEXTBYTES=1120 (=1088 ML-KEM ‖ 32 X25519), SHAREDSECRETBYTES=32, SEEDBYTES=32\nenc_deterministic seed | 64 bytes: seed[0..31] = ML-KEM m, seed[32..63] = ephemeral X25519 scalar\nkey expansion | expand_decaps_key: SHAKE256(seed,32) → 96 bytes; bytes 0..63 = ML-KEM seed, bytes 64..95 = X25519 scalar; sk is stored as the 32-byte seed and re-expanded on every dec\ncombiner | SHA3-256(ss_mlkem ‖ ss_x25519 ‖ ct_x25519 ‖ pk_x25519 ‖ xwing_label) where xwing_label = {0x5c,0x2e,0x2f,0x2f,0x5e,0x5c} (\"\\\\.//^\\\\\")\nentry points | crypto_kem_xwing_keypair vs crypto_kem_xwing_seed_keypair (deterministic); crypto_kem_xwing_enc vs crypto_kem_xwing_enc_deterministic (deterministic); crypto_kem_xwing_dec\ntop-level alias | crypto_kem_PRIMITIVE = \"xwing\"; crypto_kem_PUBLICKEYBYTES/SECRETKEYBYTES/CIPHERTEXTBYTES/SHAREDSECRETBYTES/SEEDBYTES = the xwing values (1216/32/1120/32/32); crypto_kem_{keypair,seed_keypair,enc,dec} are unconditional wrappers around crypto_kem_xwing_* (no enc_deterministic wrapper at the crypto_kem level)\n\nKX\nconstants | crypto_kx_PUBLICKEYBYTES=32, crypto_kx_SECRETKEYBYTES=32, crypto_kx_SEEDBYTES=32, crypto_kx_SESSIONKEYBYTES=32, crypto_kx_PRIMITIVE = \"x25519blake2b\"\nkeypair axes | crypto_kx_keypair (random