] &= 0x7f before frombytes; output always clears the cofactor\nfrom_hash (64 bytes, ge25519_from_hash / ristretto255_from_hash): random, all-zero, all-0xff; fe25519_reduce64 masks fl[31] and gl[31] with 0x7f and folds the dropped bits back as *19 and *722\nfrom_string / from_string_nu / scalar_from_string: hash_alg = 1 (SHA-256) and 2 (SHA-512) both valid; ctx_len <= 0xff (direct) vs ctx_len > 0xff (H2C-OVERSIZE-DST- rehash path, ctx becomes the 32/64-byte hash); ctx_len 0; msg_len 0, 1, 64, 128, 1000; the sha256 expand loop uses HASH_BYTES=32 chunks and sha512 uses 64-byte chunks; _nu produces 1 point (h_len 48), from_string produces 2 points + add (h_len 96)\nristretto255 encodings: identity = 32 zero bytes; valid canonical even encodings; s odd (rejected); s >= p (rejected); s[31] bit 7 set (rejected); non-square v*u2^2 (rejected)\nscalarmult axes: curve25519 base vs point; ed25519 clamp vs noclamp (clamp forces bit 254 set and bits 0-2 clear, so clamp+n=0 still fails via sodium_is_zero(n)); ristretto255 point vs base; ristretto255 always masks t[31] &= 127 and applies NO clamping\n\n--- sign axes ---\nmessage length: 0, 1, 31, 32, 63, 64, 65, 127, 128, 1000 (sha512 absorbs sig[0..32)+pk[0..32) = 64 bytes first, so mlen 0 and mlen 64 sit on interesting sha512 block boundaries)\nAPI shape: crypto_sign / crypto_sign_open (combined, sm = sig||m, smlen = mlen+64) vs crypto_sign_detached / crypto_sign_verify_detached\nkey derivation: crypto_sign_keypair (random seed) vs crypto_sign_seed_keypair (given 32-byte seed: 0x00*32, 0xff*32, RFC 8032 test seeds); sk layout = seed[0..32) || pk[32..64); sk_to_seed = sk[0..32); sk_to_pk = sk[32..64)\ned25519ph multi-part: init, then update chunking (0, 1, 127, 128, 129 bytes; 1 update vs N updates; zero updates at all) then final_create / final_verify; the prehash is always exactly 64 bytes and DOM2PREFIX (34 bytes) is prepended\nsignature malleability axes: S canonical vs S >= L with sig[63]&0xF0 == 0 (ACCEPTED — the guard requires the high nibble to be nonzero) vs S >= L with sig[63]&0xF0 != 0 (rejected)\nbuild-flag axes: default vs ED25519_COMPAT (changes the S/pk pre-checks) and default vs ED25519_NONDETERMINISTIC (synthetic nonce: az[0..64) plus 32 random bytes plus 32 zero bytes absorbed instead of az[32..64)); NEITHER macro is defined anywhere in this tree\nsk_to_curve25519 / pk_to_curve25519 round trip: valid keypair; pk_to_curve25519 with a small-order pk, a torsion pk, a non-canonical pk (accepted!), a non-curve pk\nverification is COFACTORED (R - (S*B - h*A) need only be small-order, not exactly identity) — so signatures differing by a torsion component still verify\n\nKEY FILE PATHS\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/ref10/open.c (lines 29-62: the whole verify gate; crypto_verify_32.h included but unused)\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_sign/ed25519/ref10/{sign.c,keypair.c}, crypto_sign/ed25519/sign_ed25519.c, crypto_sign/crypto_sign.c\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_scalarmult/{crypto_scalarmult.c,curve25519/scalarmult_curve25519.c,curve25519/ref10/x25519_ref10.c,ed25519/ref10/scalarmult_ed25519_ref10.c,ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c}\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/{core_ed25519.c,core_ristretto255.c,core_h2c.c,core_h2c.h,ref10/ed25519_ref10.c}\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_generichash/blake2b/ref/{generichash_blake2b.c,blake2b-ref.c,blake2.h}\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_hash/{sha3/hash_sha3.c,sha256/cp/hash_sha256_cp.c,sha512/cp/hash_sha512_cp.c}\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust/c_src/libsodium/crypto_xof/{shake128,sha