` mid-byte (`state==1`), e.g. `ignore=\":\"`, `\"a:bcd\"` | -1, `errno=EINVAL`, `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 7 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `bin_maxlen` exhausted, `hex_end!=NULL` | -1, `errno=ERANGE`, `*bin_len=0`, `*hex_end` at first unconsumed char | [x] |\n| 8 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `bin_maxlen` exhausted, `hex_end==NULL` | -1, `errno=EINVAL` (ERANGE overwritten), `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 9 | `sodium_hex2bin` | `bin_maxlen==0` with ≥1 valid hex digit | -1, ERANGE if `hex_end!=NULL` else EINVAL | [x] |\n| 10 | `sodium_hex2bin` | embedded NUL in `hex` with `ignore!=NULL` (`strchr(ignore,0)` matches) → NUL is SKIPPED | 0, NUL treated as ignorable (quirk) | [x] |\n\n## B. `sodium/codecs.c` — base64\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| 11 | `sodium_base64_check_variant` (via `_encoded_len`/`bin2base64`/`base642bin`) | `((unsigned)variant & ~0x6) != 0x1`, i.e. variant ∉ {1,3,5,7} — tested 0,2,4,6,8,9,99,0xFFFFFFFF | misuse | [x] |\n| 12 | `sodium_base64_encoded_len` | `bin_len/3 > (SIZE_MAX-5)/4` | misuse | [x] |\n| 13 | `sodium_bin2base64` | `bin_len/3 > (SIZE_MAX-5)/4` | misuse | [x] |\n| 14 | `sodium_bin2base64` | `b64_maxlen <= required b64_len` | misuse | [x] |\n| 15 | `sodium_base642bin` | invalid b64 char not in `ignore`, `b64_end==NULL`, not at `b64_len` | -1, `errno=EINVAL`, `*bin_len` may be NONZERO (partial decode kept) | [x] |\n| 16 | `sodium_base642bin` | invalid char where padding expected (padded variant, `skip_padding` sees non-`=`) | -1, `errno=EINVAL`, `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 17 | `sodium_base642bin` | invalid char, `b64_end!=NULL`, no padding obligation | **0**, `*b64_end` at bad char, `*bin_len`=prefix | [x] |\n| 18 | `sodium_base642bin` | one leftover b64 char (`consumed % 4 == 1` ⇒ `acc_len==6`), e.g. `\"A\"` | -1, **errno UNCHANGED** (no assignment on this branch), `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 19 | `sodium_base642bin` | nonzero trailing bits, e.g. `\"AC\"` | -1, **errno UNCHANGED**, `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 20 | `sodium_base642bin` | `bin_maxlen` exceeded, `b64_end!=NULL` | -1, `errno=ERANGE`, `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 21 | `sodium_base642bin` | `bin_maxlen` exceeded, `b64_end==NULL` | -1, `errno=EINVAL` (ERANGE overwritten), `*bin_len=0` | [x] |\n| 22 | `sodium_base642bin` | `bin_maxlen==0` with decodable data | -1, ERANGE or EINVAL as above | [x] |\n| 23 | `sodium_base642bin` | PADDED variant (1,5), padding absent/truncated: `\"/w\"`, `\"/wE\"` | -1, `errno=ERANGE` (from `skip_padding` overrun — NOT EINVAL) | [x] |\n| 24 | `sodium_base642bin` | NO_PADDING variant (3,7) fed padded `\"/w==\"`, `b64_end==NULL` | -1, `errno=EINVAL`, `*bin_len` NONZERO | [x] |\n| 25 | `sodium_base642bin` | NO_PADDING variant fed padded input, `b64_end!=NULL` | **0**, `*b64_end` at first `=` | [x] |\n| 26 | `sodium_base642bin` | URLSAFE variant (5,7) fed `'+'` or `'/'` | invalid char → row 15/17 behaviour | [x] |\n| 27 | `sodium_base642bin` | ORIGINAL variant (1,3) fed `'-'` or `'_'` | invalid char → row 15/17/23 behaviour | [x] |\n| 28 | `sodium_base642bin` | `ignore` CONTAINS `'='` with a padded variant, `\"/w==\"`, `ignore=\"=\"` | -1, `errno=ERANGE`, `*bin_len=0` (quirk) | [x] |\n| 29 | `sodium_base642bin` | extra `'='` beyond required padding `\"/w===\"`, `b64_end==NULL` | -1, `errno=EINVAL` | [x] |\n| 30 | `sodium_base642bin` | `b64_end==NULL` and any unconsumed trailing byte | -1, `errno=EINVAL` | [x] |\n\n## C. `sodium/codecs.c` — IP parsing\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| 31 | `sodium_ip2bin` | `'%'` zone with a char outside `[0-9a-zA-Z._-]`, e.g. `\"fe80::1%bad!\"` | -1 | [x] |\n| 32 | `sodium_ip2bin` | `'%'` with empty zone, `\"fe80::1%\"` | -1 | [x] |\n| 33 | `sodium_ip2bin` | `'%'` zone but address has no `':'`, `\"1.2.3.4%eth0\"` | -1 | [x] |\n| 34 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv4 octet > 255 (`\"256.0.0.1\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 35 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv4 with > 3 digits in an octet (`\"1234.1.1.1\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 36 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv4 missing octet (`\"1.2.3\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 37 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv4 extra octet (`\"1.2.3.4.5\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 38 | `sodium_ip2bin` | empty string `\"\"` or `\".\"` | -1 | [x] |\n| 39 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv6 group with > 4 hex digits (`\"12345::\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 40 | `sodium_ip2bin` | IPv6 non-hex char (`\"g::1\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 41 | `sodium_ip2bin` | single leading `':'` not followed by `':'` (`\":1\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 42 | `sodium_ip2bin` | trailing single `':'` (`\"1:\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 43 | `sodium_ip2bin` | two `\"::\"` runs (`\"2001:db8::1::2\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 44 | `sodium_ip2bin` | more than 8 IPv6 groups (`\"1:2:3:4:5:6:7:8:9\"`) | -1 | [x] |\n| 45 | `sodium_ip2bin` | `\"::\"` when 16 bytes already filled | -1 | [x] |\n| 46 | `sodium_bin2ip` | `ip_maxlen <= 2` | NULL | [x] |\n| 47 | `sodium_bin2ip` | formatted length `>= ip_maxlen` | NULL | [x] |\n\n## D. `sodium/utils.c` — pad / unpad / compare / alloc\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| 48 | `sodium_pad` | `blocksize == 0` | -1, `*padded_buflen_p` NOT written | [x] |\n| 49 | `sodium_pad` | `SIZE_MAX - unpadded_buflen <= xpadlen` (arith overflow) | **misuse** (not -1) | [x] |\n| 50 | `sodium_pad` | `xpadded_len >= max_buflen` | -1, `*padded_buflen_p` NOT written | [x] |\n| 51 | `sodium_unpad` | `blocksize == 0` | -1, `*unpadded_buflen_p` NOT written | [x] |\n| 52 | `sodium_unpad` | `padded_buflen < blocksize` | -1, `*unpadded_buflen_p` NOT written | [x] |\n| 53 | `sodium_unpad` | no `0x80` barrier preceded only by `0x00`s in the last `blocksize` bytes (all-zero, all-0xff, `0x81` terminator, nonzero after barrier) | -1 **AND** `*unpadded_buflen_p = padded_buflen-1` IS written | [x] |\n| 54 | `sodium_malloc` | `size >= SIZE_MAX - page_size*4` (HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC) | NULL, `errno=ENOMEM` | [x] |\n| 55 | `sodium_allocarray` | `count > 0 && size >= SIZE_MAX / count` | NULL, `errno=ENOMEM` | [x] |\n| 56 | `sodium_free` | `ptr == NULL` | no-op | [x] |\n| 57 | `sodium_mprotect_noaccess` | build without HAVE_PAGE_PROTECTION | -1, `errno=ENOSYS` | [x] |\n| 58 | `sodium_mprotect_readonly` | build without HAVE_PAGE_PROTECTION | -1, `errno=ENOSYS` | [x] |\n| 59 | `sodium_mprotect_readwrite` | build without HAVE_PAGE_PROTECTION | -1, `errno=ENOSYS` | [x] |\n| 60 | `sodium_mlock` | no HAVE_MLOCK, or `mlock()` fails (RLIMIT_MEMLOCK/EPERM) | -1 | [x] |\n| 61 | `sodium_munlock` | as `sodium_mlock`; zeroes region first | -1 | [x] |\n| 62 | `sodium_memcmp` | any of `len` bytes differ | -1 (0 if equal; `len==0` → 0) | [x] |\n| 63 | `sodium_compare` | little-endian `b1 < b2` / `>` | -1 / 1 (0 if equal; `len==0` → 0) | [x] |\n| 64 | `sodium_is_zero` | any nonzero byte | 0 (1 if all zero; `nlen==0` → 1) | [x] |\n\n## E. `sodium/core.c`, `runtime.c`, `version.c`\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| 65 | `sodium_init` | any call after the first successful one | 1 | [x] |\n| 66 | `sodium_init` | `sodium_crit_enter()`/`_leave()` failure | -1 | [x] |\n| 67 | `sodium_crit_leave` | called while `locked == 0` | -1, `errno=EPERM` | [x] |\n| 68 | `sodium_misuse` | always | handler (if set) then unconditional `abort()`; `noreturn` — a handler that RETURNS still aborts | [x] |\n| 69 | `sodium_set_misuse_handler` | `handler == NULL` | **0** (valid — clears the handler) | [x] |\n| 70 | `sodium_runtime_has_*` (12 fns) | called before `sodium_init()` | 0 (static zero-init `CPUFeatures`) | [x] |\n\n## F. `randombytes/`\n\n| # | function | trigger | expected C result | [ ] |\n|---|----------|---------|-------------------|-----|\n| 71 | `randombytes_set_implementation` | any impl (never validated) | 0 | [x] |\n| 72 | `randombytes_set_implementation` | `NULL` (declared nonnull) | 0; impl becomes NULL ⇒ next call resets to `&randombytes_sysrandom_implementation` + stirs | [x] |\n| 73 | `random