{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Dcac6wc3N2i8Yp6Em2gVCq","type":"tool_result","content":"# CONFIGS.md — Phase A: CONFIGURATION-SURFACE TABLE\n\nThe mirror of `ERRORS.md` for **valid** inputs. Axes were derived mechanically\nfrom the C source: every runtime option/mode/flag the public API can set, every\ninput SHAPE the code special-cases, and the FULL set of public entry points —\nincluding the lowest-level ones, not just the one-shot convenience wrappers.\n\nOne row per meaningful COMBINATION the C treats differently. Each row is driven\nwith MANY randomized inputs (fixed seed `0x5EED_1234`, ≥64 iterations/row unless\nnoted) through BOTH `.so` files and compared byte-for-byte.\n\n## Build configuration\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` section**, so the crate has exactly ONE\nconfiguration. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` defines **no `HAVE_*` macros**, so every\n`#ifdef HAVE_*` in the C selects the portable fallback (equivalent to\n`configure --disable-asm`). Consequences that the table below relies on:\n\n| axis | value in this build |\n|---|---|\n=====ROWS 50-90=====\n115:| 50 | `randombytes_uniform` | **[RNG]** injected impl, `uniform=NULL` ⇒ exercises libsodium's own rejection sampler; `upper_bound` ∈ {0,1,2,3,7,0x7fffffff,0x80000001,0xffffffff} | [ ] |\n116:| 51 | `randombytes_uniform` | **[RNG]** injected impl WITH `uniform != NULL` ⇒ delegation path, incl. bound 0/1 | [ ] |\n117:| 52 | `randombytes_stir` / `_close` | idempotency; `close` with `impl->close == NULL` | [ ] |\n118:| 53 | `randombytes` (NaCl compat) + `randombytes_internal_implementation` | name `\"internal\"`, `uniform=NULL` | [ ] |\n124:| 54 | `crypto_verify_16` / `_32` / `_64` | equal buffers; differ at each byte position; all-0x00 vs all-0xff | [ ] |\n125:| 55 | `crypto_shorthash_siphash24` | `inlen` ∈ {0,1,7,8,9,15,16,17,63,64,65,1000}; key all-0x00 / all-0xff / random | [ ] |\n126:| 56 | `crypto_shorthash_siphashx24` | same shapes (16-byte output) | [ ] |\n127:| 57 | `crypto_shorthash` (dispatch) + `_bytes`/`_keybytes`/`_primitive` | delegates to siphash24 | [ ] |\n133:| 58 | `crypto_hash_sha256` one-shot | `mlen` ∈ {0,1,55,**56**,63,**64**,65,111,112,119,120,127,128,191,192,1000} (pad boundary `r==56`) | [ ] |\n134:| 59 | `crypto_hash_sha256_init/_update/_final` | single update; must equal row 58 | [ ] |\n135:| 60 | `crypto_hash_sha256_*` | multi-update chunking: `inlen < 64-r` small path, exact-fill, `while (inlen >= 64)` loop, `inlen &= 63` tail; `inlen==0` no-op | [ ] |\n136:| 61 | `crypto_hash_sha512` one-shot | `mlen` ∈ {0,1,111,**112**,119,120,127,**128**,129,239,240,255,256,1000} (pad boundary `r==112`) | [ ] |\n137:| 62 | `crypto_hash_sha512_init/_update/_final` | single and multi-update chunking as row 60 (block 128) | [ ] |\n138:| 63 | `crypto_hash` / `_bytes` / `_primitive` | dispatch to sha512 (`\"sha512\"`) | [ ] |\n139:| 64 | `crypto_hash_sha3256` one-shot | rate **136**, `mlen` ∈ {0,1,**135**,**136**,137,143,144,271,272,1000} | [ ] |\n140:| 65 | `crypto_hash_sha3512` one-shot | rate **72**, `mlen` ∈ {0,1,**71**,**72**,73,143,144,1000} | [ ] |\n141:| 66 | `crypto_hash_sha3256_init/_update/_final` | `offset != 0` partial-fill branch; `while (inlen-consumed >= rate)` loop leaving `offset == rate`; trailing remainder | [ ] |\n142:| 67 | `crypto_hash_sha3512_init/_update/_final` | same three branches at rate 72 | [ ] |\n148:| 68 | `crypto_xof_shake128` one-shot | rate **168**; `outlen` ∈ {0,1,167,168,169,336,337,504,1000} × `inlen` ∈ {0,1,167,168,169,337} | [ ] |\n149:| 69 | `crypto_xof_shake256` one-shot | rate **136**; `outlen`/`inlen` at {0,1,135,136,137,272,273,1000} | [ ] |\n150:| 70 | `crypto_xof_turboshake128` one-shot | rate **168**, **12-round** permute; same shape set | [ ] |\n151:| 71 | `crypto_xof_turboshake256` one-shot | rate **136**, **12-round** permute; same shape set | [ ] |\n152:| 72 | `_init` / `_update` / `_squeeze` (all 4) | multi-squeeze: `squeeze(rate)`×2 == `squeeze(2*rate)`; `squeeze(1)`×N == `squeeze(N)` (resume mid-block) | [ ] |\n153:| 73 | `_init` / `_update` / `_squeeze` (all 4) | absorb chunking straddling a rate boundary; multi-update splits | [ ] |\n154:| 74 | `_init_with_domain` (all 4) | domain byte ∈ {0x00,0x01,0x06,0x07,0x1F,0x7F,**0x80**,0xFF} — no validation; 0x80 collides with the pad bit | [ ] |\n155:| 75 | `_init_with_domain` (all 4) | padding-branch axis: `offset == rate-1` (single combined `domain^0x80`) vs `offset < rate-1` vs `offset == rate` | [ ] |\n156:| 76 | `_blockbytes` / `_statebytes` / `_domain_standard` (all 4) | 168/136, 256, 0x1F | [ ] |\n162:| 77 | `crypto_core_salsa20` | `c == NULL` (sigma) vs explicit 16-byte constants; key/in all-0x00, all-0xff, random | [ ] |\n163:| 78 | `crypto_core_salsa2012` (12 rounds) | same axes | [ ] |\n164:| 79 | `crypto_core_salsa208` (8 rounds) | same axes | [ ] |\n165:| 80 | `crypto_core_hsalsa20` | `c == NULL` vs explicit; out 32, in 16, k 32 | [ ] |\n166:| 81 | `crypto_core_hchacha20` | `c == NULL` vs explicit; out 32, in 16, k 32 | [ ] |\n167:| 82 | `crypto_core_keccak1600_init/_xor_bytes/_extract_bytes` | offset/length combos within 200 bytes; `_permute_24` vs `_permute_12` | [ ] |\n173:| 83 | `crypto_stream_chacha20` (keystream) | 8-byte nonce; `clen` ∈ {0,1,31,32,63,**64**,65,127,128,129,191,192,255,256,512,513,1024,4096} | [ ] |\n174:| 84 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_xor` | same lengths; in-place `c==m` and disjoint | [ ] |\n175:| 85 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_xor_ic` | `ic` (u64) ∈ {0,1,**2^32-1**,**2^32**,2^32+1, 2^64-1} — exercises the `j12` wrap into `j13` | [ ] |\n176:| 86 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf` | 12-byte nonce; same length set | [ ] |\n177:| 87 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor` | same lengths | [ ] |\n178:| 88 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_xor_ic` | `ic` (u32) ∈ {0,1,2^32-2,2^32-1} and the guard boundary `ic == 2^32-ceil(mlen/64)` (last legal) | [ ] |\n179:| 89 | `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_ext` / `_ext_xor_ic` | extended-counter low-level entry points; same lengths | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VzwhJ8wTQF9hPfSP9dc71s","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"88db5bc9-5afe-4ef1-9b16-2b0549eea1ef","timestamp":"2026-08-14T16:46:39.477Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write hash/xof/core tests"}
