.txt` defines no `HAVE_*` macros (`flags.make` = `-Dsodium_EXPORTS` only; `nm -D --undefined-only` shows no `pthread_*`), so core.c compiles the final `#else` branch where both helpers `return 0` and `locked` is never touched. The Rust had translated the `HAVE_PTHREAD` branch instead.\n\nNo other `src/` file was changed (`src/utils.rs` and `src/randombytes.rs` were temporarily mutated for a vacuity check and restored byte-identically — `diff` clean).\n\n**Mutation check (proves the tests are not vacuous):** breaking three Rust functions (12-byte `sodium_increment` fast path, `sodium_unpad`'s unconditional out-param write, `randombytes_uniform`'s `min`) made exactly `cfg38`, `err53`, `cfg50` fail and nothing else.\n\n## (d) Rows whose documented branch is unreachable in this build (each still gets a C-vs-Rust assertion of the reachable behaviour, and the reason is a comment in the test)\n- **ERRORS 54** — the `size >= SIZE_MAX - page_size*4` pre-check lives inside `#ifdef HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC`, undefined here (plain `malloc` path). Tested the reachable equivalent: 69 huge sizes → NULL + `errno=ENOMEM`, identical in both.\n- **ERRORS 66** — `sodium_init() == -1` requires `sodium_crit_enter/leave` to fail; in the `#else` branch they cannot. Asserted both helpers return 0 and `sodium_init` never returns −1 in either library.\n- **ERRORS 79** — the `-1` from a second `/dev/urandom` close is unreachable because `getrandom(2)` exists on this kernel, so `stream.getrandom_available != 0` forces `0`. Repeated `randombytes_close()` return values + errno are still compared call-by-call.\n- **ERRORS 76 (latent, not observable)** — `src/randombytes.rs` omits the C's explicit `size > 0x4000000000` → `sodium_misuse()` check, but the downstream `crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf` in *both* libraries performs the identical `clen > crypto_stream_chacha20_ietf_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` (= 64·2³² = 0x4000000000) misuse check, so both abort at exactly the same threshold. The test passes with no `src/` edit; flagging it in case you want the redundant check added for literal fidelity.\n\n**Build caveat for the caller:** `cargo test --test t02_utils` does **not** rebuild the cdylib that the harness `dlopen`s — run `cargo build` first after any `src/` change (I hit a stale-`.so` false failure this way). Also note `tests/t01_codecs.rs` (another agent's in-flight file) currently fails, so a bare `cargo test` aborts before reaching t02; run per test target.","usage":{"total_tokens":201139,"tool_uses":63,"duration_ms":1750390},"uuid":"556702cc-cd43-4533-90d7-f4aeabb2affa","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051"}
