{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_auvj4dvx3ffdctip4cmetetwd25jhxwwuqapkihvfranimdipgsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_013xj565Xgh7bG77qAPP4THZ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write MAC/generichash tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Write ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust differential verification of libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nREPO: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nYOUR FILE (create it, nothing else): tests/t05_mac.rs\n\n## HARD RULES\n- Do NOT modify: `c_src/**` (the C is ground truth), `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, `run_difftests.sh`, or any other `tests/t*.rs`.\n- You MAY read anything. You MAY edit files under `src/` ONLY to fix a genuine Rust translation bug proven by a failing differential test.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — every call goes through `dlsym` on BOTH shared libraries via the harness. This is what tests the `#[no_mangle]` export wrappers.\n- NEVER weaken/skip an assertion. The C is ALWAYS correct. If C and Rust disagree, the RUST is wrong.\n\n## BUILD (critical — read this)\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib for integration tests. ALWAYS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nulimit -c 0        # otherwise intentional SIGABRTs get core-dumped: 100x slowdown\ncargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test t05_mac 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\n(The harness now hard-fails if the `.so` is older than `src/**.rs`, but build anyway.)\n\n## THE HARNESS (tests/common/mod.rs — READ IT FIRST)\n```rust\nmod common; use common::*;\ninit_both();\nlet (c, r) = fnpair!(\"symbol_name\", unsafe extern \"C\" fn(A,B)->R);\nunsafe { pair::<T>(\"name\") }\nassert_eq_bytes(\"what\", &c_out, &r_out);\nRng::new(SEED)   // .bytes(n) .byte() .next_u32() .below(n) .fill(&mut b) .pick(&xs)\npub const LENS: &[usize]; pub fn patterns(n, &mut rng) -> Vec<Vec<u8>>\nforked(|| -> i64 { ... }) -> Outcome; Outcome::Signaled(SIGABRT); assert_same_fatal(..)\ninstall_det_rng(bool); reset_det_rng();\nlibs(); sym::<T>(&libs().c, \"name\")\n```\n**Fork hygiene** (learned the hard way — a forked child of a multi-threaded test process deadlocks on the loader/malloc lock): resolve all symbols and allocate ALL buffers in the PARENT, before `forked(...)`; inside the child closure only call an already-resolved function pointer. Also `libc::setrlimit(RLIMIT_CORE, 0)` in tests that fork a lot.\n**Parallelism**: cargo runs tests as parallel threads sharing ONE pair of `.so`s. Any test that calls `install_det_rng` mutates global state in both libs — guard those with a file-local `std::sync::Mutex` and restore the default implementation afterwards.\n\n## WHAT TO COVER\nRead `CONFIGS.md` rows **98–121** and `ERRORS.md` rows **154–161** and **222–236** — they are your specification.\n\n**poly1305 / onetimeauth** (CONFIGS 98–102, ERRORS 161):\n`crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305`, `_verify`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_statebytes`, `_keygen`; `crypto_onetimeauth`, `_verify`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`, `_statebytes`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_primitive`; `_crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_pick_best_implementation`.\nThe leftover-buffer axis is the whole point: block_size is **16** for the donna impl selected in this build. Cover all 5 branches of `poly1305_update`: (a) `leftover==0 && bytes<16`; (b) `leftover!=0 && want>bytes` (top-up only, early return); (c) top-up exactly fills the buffer; (d) `bytes>=16` bulk path; (e) nonzero remainder stored back. Chunkings: 1+15, 15+1, 16 in one call, 16 in two calls, 17, 31+1, 32, 33, and a 0-length update. `_final`: `leftover==0` vs `leftover` in 1..15.\n\n**HMAC** (CONFIGS 103–110, ERRORS 154–160):\n`crypto_auth_hmacsha256_{init,update,final,verify,keygen,bytes,keybytes,statebytes}` + `crypto_auth_hmacsha256`; same for `hmacsha512` and `hmacsha512256`; `crypto_auth`, `_verify`, `_keygen`, `_bytes`, `_keybytes`, `_primitive`.\nThe KEY-LENGTH axis in `_init` is the main config axis. sha256 block=**64**, sha512/512256 block=**128**. Cover keylen ∈ {0 (with key=NULL — legal), 1, 32, block (exact), block+1 (**key gets PRE-HASHED with state->ictx**), 2*block}. ERRORS 154–156: `key==NULL && 0 < keylen <= block` → `sodium_misuse()` → SIGABRT in BOTH libs (use `forked`).\n\n**BLAKE2b / generichash** (CONFIGS 111–121, ERRORS 222–236):\n`crypto_generichash_blake2b`, `_salt_personal`, `_init`, `_init_salt_personal`, `_update`, `_final`, `_keygen`, `_statebytes`, `_bytes`, `_bytes_min`, `_bytes_max`, `_keybytes`, `_keybytes_min`, `_keybytes_max`, `_saltbytes`, `_personalbytes`; `crypto_generichash`, `_init`, `_update`, `_final`, `_keygen`, `_statebytes`(==384), `_bytes*`, `_keybytes*`, `_primitive`; `_crypto_generichash_blake2b_pick_best_implementation`.\nCritical facts (from the C, already verified):\n- `outlen` 1..15 and `keylen` 1..15 are **ACCEPTED** — `BYTES_MIN`/`KEYBYTES_MIN` (16) are NOT enforced. Only `outlen==0`, `outlen>64`, `keylen>64` return -1.\n- `crypto_generichash_blake2b_final` with a bad `(uint8_t)outlen` (0 or >64) hits `blake2b_final`'s guard → **`sodium_misuse()`/abort**, NOT -1. Use `forked`.\n- `_final` called twice → `blake2b_is_lastblock` → **-1**.\n- `_final`'s `outlen` is NOT checked against `_init`'s; a mismatch silently returns 0 with a different digest. Assert C and Rust agree.\n- `key == NULL` with `keylen > 0` at the `crypto_generichash_blake2b_init` wrapper takes the UNKEYED path (no misuse).\n- BLAKE2B_BLOCKBYTES=128 and the state buffer is **256** bytes; `_update`'s branch is `inlen > 256 - buflen`. The keyed path pre-absorbs one zero-padded 128-byte block so the initial `buflen` is 128. `_final`'s extra-compress fires only when `buflen > 128`. Sweep `inlen` ∈ {0,1,127,128,129,255,256,257,383,384} and multi-update splits 1+1, 63+65, 127+1, 128+128, 1x256, 256x1.\n- salt/personal are 16 bytes each; `salt==NULL` and/or `personal==NULL` are legal (zero-filled). Distinct salt or personal must change the digest.\n\nC sources: `c_src/libsodium/crypto_onetimeauth/**`, `crypto_auth/**`, `crypto_generichash/**`. Headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`. READ them for exact signatures and state sizes.\n\n### Requirements\n1. **Every** CONFIGS row 98–121 gets a `#[test]` (or clearly-named section) driving ≥64 randomized inputs.\n2. **Every** ERRORS row 154–161, 222–236 gets a C-vs-Rust assertion on the return value AND the output bytes (abort rows via `forked` + `assert_same_fatal`, and assert the outcome really is `Signaled(SIGABRT)` so the row cannot pass vacuously).\n3. Allocate opaque states via the library's own `*_statebytes()` where available, else the header struct size; use a generously oversized 64-byte-aligned buffer prefilled with 0xAA and compare the WHOLE state buffer between libs after `_init` and after each `_update` — that catches state-layout divergence, which is invisible if you only compare the final digest.\n4. Streaming must equal one-shot in BOTH libs, and C must equal Rust.\n5. `*_verify`: correct tag; tag corrupted at EVERY byte position.\n6. Prefill output buffers with 0xAA plus a trailing guard; compare the FULL buffer and assert the guard is intact.\n7. `*_keygen` rows need `install_det_rng` — hold the mutex and restore afterwards.\n\n## ON DIVERGENCE\n1. Print exact inputs (key, keylen, outlen, message, chunking) and the first differing byte offset.\n2. Rust sources: `src/primitives/{poly1305,onetimeauth,blake2b,generichash}.rs`, `src/aead/auth.rs`, `src/aead/generichash_dispatch.rs`.\n3. Fix the Rust to match the C EXACTLY, including the quirks listed above.\n4. Re-run and confirm.\n5. Report EVERY `src/` edit with a one-line before/after and the proving row.\n\n## DELIVERABLE\n`tests/t05_mac.rs` compiling and PASSING. Report: (a) test count, (b) CONFIGS/ERRORS rows → test fn mapping, (c) every `src/` fix with the proving row, (d) any row not covered and precisely why. Also state whether you ran a mutation check (deliberately break a Rust fn, confirm a test catches it, revert) — do at least 5."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":229637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":629,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"a996926d-1fa5-4b82-aad3-973e81a51fb6","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:37:34.359Z"}
