{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_auvj4dvx3ffdctip4cmetetwd25jhxwwuqapkihvfranimdipgsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01S9M9n7rkngWNWV4hpar9rp","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write curve/sign tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Write ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust differential verification of libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nREPO: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nYOUR FILE (create it, nothing else): tests/t06_curve.rs\n\n## HARD RULES\n- Do NOT modify: `c_src/**` (the C is ground truth), `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, `run_difftests.sh`, or any other `tests/t*.rs`.\n- You MAY read anything. You MAY edit files under `src/` ONLY to fix a genuine Rust translation bug proven by a failing differential test.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — every call goes through `dlsym` on BOTH shared libraries via the harness.\n- NEVER weaken/skip an assertion. The C is ALWAYS correct. If C and Rust disagree, the RUST is wrong.\n\n## BUILD (critical)\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib for integration tests. ALWAYS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nulimit -c 0\ncargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test t06_curve 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\n\n## THE HARNESS (tests/common/mod.rs — READ IT FIRST)\n```rust\nmod common; use common::*;\ninit_both();\nlet (c, r) = fnpair!(\"symbol_name\", unsafe extern \"C\" fn(A,B)->R);\nassert_eq_bytes(\"what\", &c_out, &r_out);\nRng::new(SEED)   // .bytes(n) .byte() .next_u32() .below(n) .fill(&mut b) .pick(&xs)\nforked(|| -> i64 { ... }) -> Outcome; Outcome::Signaled(SIGABRT); assert_same_fatal(..)\ninstall_det_rng(bool); reset_det_rng();\nlibs(); sym::<T>(&libs().c, \"name\")\n```\n**Fork hygiene**: resolve symbols and allocate buffers in the PARENT; the child closure only calls a pre-resolved fn pointer. `setrlimit(RLIMIT_CORE,0)` in fork-heavy tests.\n**Parallelism**: tests are parallel threads sharing one pair of `.so`s; guard `install_det_rng` users with a file-local `Mutex` and restore the default impl after.\n\n## WHAT TO COVER\nRead `CONFIGS.md` rows **122–163** and `ERRORS.md` rows **162–221** — they are your specification. This is the elliptic-curve surface:\n\n- `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519`, `_curve25519_base`, `crypto_scalarmult`, `_base`, `_bytes`, `_scalarbytes`, `_primitive`, `_crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_pick_best_implementation`\n- `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519`, `_ed25519_noclamp`, `_ed25519_base`, `_ed25519_base_noclamp`, `_ed25519_bytes`, `_ed25519_scalarbytes`\n- `crypto_scalarmult_ristretto255`, `_ristretto255_base`, `_ristretto255_bytes`, `_ristretto255_scalarbytes`\n- `crypto_core_ed25519_is_valid_point`, `_add`, `_sub`, `_from_uniform`, `_from_hash`, `_random`, `_from_string`, `_from_string_nu`, `_scalar_from_string`, `_scalar_random`, `_scalar_reduce`, `_scalar_negate`, `_scalar_complement`, `_scalar_add`, `_scalar_sub`, `_scalar_mul`, `_scalar_invert`, `_scalar_is_canonical`, and all `*bytes` getters\n- the whole matching `crypto_core_ristretto255_*` set\n- `crypto_sign_ed25519_{keypair,seed_keypair,detached,verify_detached,open,sk_to_seed,sk_to_pk,sk_to_curve25519,pk_to_curve25519}`, `crypto_sign_ed25519`, `crypto_sign_ed25519ph_{init,update,final_create,final_verify}`, `crypto_sign_ed25519ph_statebytes`, and the `crypto_sign_*` dispatch layer + all constant getters\n\nC sources: `c_src/libsodium/crypto_scalarmult/**`, `crypto_core/ed25519/**`, `crypto_sign/**`. Headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`. READ them for exact signatures.\n\n### Test-vector construction (do this carefully — it is most of the work)\nYou need real curve points and scalars. Build them USING THE C LIBRARY ITSELF (that is legitimate: it is ground truth), then feed the same bytes to both libs:\n- valid main-subgroup ed25519 points: `crypto_core_ed25519_from_uniform` / `_random`, or a public key from `crypto_sign_ed25519_keypair`.\n- the **8 small-order** ed25519 points and the curve25519 **7 blocklisted** encodings: read them out of the C source (`ge25519_has_small_order`'s table in `c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10/ed25519_ref10.c` and `has_small_order`'s table in `c_src/libsodium/crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/ref10/x25519_ref10.c`) and hard-code them.\n- non-canonical encodings: y = p, p+1, 2^255-1 (p = 2^255-19).\n- a torsion point (on the curve, NOT in the main subgroup): add a small-order point to a valid point with `crypto_core_ed25519_add` (which accepts them).\n- the group order L = 2^252 + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493, little-endian bytes: `ed d3 f5 5c 1a 63 12 58 d6 9c f7 a2 de f9 de 14` then 15 zeros then `10`. Scalars to sweep: 0, 1, 2, 8, L-1, L, L+1, 2^252, 2^255-1, 2^256-1, random.\n- valid ristretto255 encodings: `crypto_core_ristretto255_random` / `_from_hash`. Invalid: `s` odd, `s >= p`, bit 255 set, a non-square.\n\n### Critical C behaviours the Rust must match (from the verified error table)\n- ed25519 signature verification is **COFACTORED**: the final check is `ge25519_has_small_order(&check) - 1` where `check = R - (S*B - h*A)`. `crypto_verify_32` is `#include`d in `open.c` but **never called**. A signature differing by a torsion component still verifies (CONFIGS 163).\n- Malleability (CONFIGS 162): `S >= L` with `sig[63] & 0xF0 == 0` is **ACCEPTED**; `S >= L` with `sig[63] & 0xF0 != 0` is rejected. Construct all three cases.\n- `crypto_sign_ed25519_pk_to_curve25519` does **NOT** call `ge25519_is_canonical` — non-canonical pk is ACCEPTED (ERRORS 177).\n- `crypto_core_ed25519_add`/`_sub` gate ONLY on `frombytes` + `is_on_curve` — non-canonical, small-order and torsion points are ACCEPTED (ERRORS 207). Contrast with `_is_valid_point` and `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519`, which apply the full 4/5-check gate.\n- `crypto_scalarmult_ed25519*`: `sodium_is_zero(n,32)` is checked AFTER the multiply, on the ORIGINAL unclamped `n` (ERRORS 189/191).\n- `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_base` has **NO** rejection branch at all (ERRORS 183).\n- `crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_invert(0)` returns -1 but `recip` IS still written by `sc25519_invert` before the check (ERRORS 210) — compare the OUTPUT BUFFER too, not just the return code.\n- `hash_alg` ∉ {1,2} for every `_from_string*` → -1 + `errno=EINVAL`. Test 0, 3, -1, 255, 0x7fffffff — out-of-range enums crossing FFI (ERRORS 209/218/221).\n- `ctx_len > 0xff` triggers the `H2C-OVERSIZE-DST-` rehash path (CONFIGS 142–144, 150).\n\n### Requirements\n1. **Every** CONFIGS row 122–163 gets a `#[test]` (or clearly-named section) driving ≥64 randomized inputs where a random shape exists.\n2. **Every** ERRORS row 162–221 gets a C-vs-Rust assertion on the return value AND the full output buffer AND errno where applicable.\n3. Prefill every output buffer with 0xAA plus a trailing guard; compare the FULL buffer.\n4. Algebraic properties, asserted in BOTH libs and compared across libs: X25519 ECDH agreement; `scalar_invert(s)*s == 1 mod L`; `negate(negate(s)) == s`; `complement(s) + s == 1 mod L`; sign→verify round-trip; `sk_to_pk`/`sk_to_seed` consistency; clamp vs noclamp must DIFFER.\n5. ed25519ph: update chunking {0,1,127,128,129} × {1 update, N updates, ZERO updates}.\n\n## ON DIVERGENCE\n1. Print exact inputs and the first differing byte offset.\n2. Rust sources: `src/ed25519/{fe25519,ge25519,sc25519,base,base2,scalarmult,sign,x25519,ristretto255,core_ed25519,core_ristretto255,h2c,sha512}.rs`.\n3. Fix the Rust to match the C EXACTLY. Field-arithmetic carry handling and the canonicality/small-order tables are the usual culprits.\n4. Re-run and confirm.\n5. Report EVERY `src/` edit with a one-line before/after and the proving row.\n\n## DELIVERABLE\n`tests/t06_curve.rs` compiling and PASSING. Report: (a) test count, (b) CONFIGS/ERRORS rows → test fn mapping, (c) every `src/` fix with the proving row, (d) any row not covered and precisely why. Also run ≥5 mutation checks (break a Rust fn, confirm a test catches it, revert) and report them."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":229637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":629,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"5069ec4a-ed2c-406f-9e6c-958234fa993b","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:38:10.758Z"}
