pt_detached` | same cross-product; separate MAC buffer | [ ] |\n286:| 166 | `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_*` | `mlen` = **131072** (`STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK`) and **131073** (chunk+1, exercises the 64-bit `ic` carry; decrypt does a SINGLE `xor_ic`) | [ ] |\n287:| 167 | `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt` / `_decrypt` (12-byte nonce, **RFC 8439** layout with `_pad0`) | `mlen` ∈ {0,1,**15**,**16**,17,63,64,65,1000} × `adlen` ∈ {0,1,**15**,**16**,17} (pad is 0 exactly at %16==0) | [ ] |\n288:| 168 | `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt_detached` / `_decrypt_detached` | same cross-product | [ ] |\n289:| 169 | `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf_*` | `mlen` = 131072 / 131073 (u32 `ic`) | [ ] |\n290:| 170 | `crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt` / `_decrypt` (24-byte nonce, HChacha20 sub-key, `npub2 = 4 zero bytes \\|\\| npub[16..24)`) | `mlen` × `adlen` as row 167 | [ ] |\n291:| 171 | `crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_encrypt_detached` / `_decrypt_detached` | same cross-product | [ ] |\n292:| 172 | all rows 164–171 | `ad == NULL` with `adlen == 0`; `nsec != NULL`; in-place `c == m`; `*clen_p`/`*maclen_p`/`*mlen_p` NULL | [ ] |\n293:| 173 | `*_decrypt_detached` with `m == NULL` | verify-only mode (distinct code path) for all 4 variants | [ ] |\n294:| 174 | `*_keygen` (all 4) + `_keybytes`/`_nsecbytes`/`_npubbytes`/`_abytes`/`_messagebytes_max` | **[RNG]** + constant getters, incl. the uppercase `_IETF_*` aliases | [ ] |\n300:| 175 | `crypto_aead_aegis128l_encrypt` / `_decrypt` | RATE **32**; `mlen` ∈ {0,1,31,**32**,33,**64**,65,1000} × `adlen` ∈ {0,1,31,**32**,33,63,**64**,65,127,128} (absorb vs absorb2 `2*RATE` fast path) | [ ] |\n301:| 176 | `crypto_aead_aegis128l_encrypt_detached` / `_decrypt_detached` | same cross-product; `m == NULL` scratch-decrypt path | [ ] |\n302:| 177 | `crypto_aead_aegis256_encrypt` / `_decrypt` | RATE **16**; `mlen` ∈ {0,1,15,**16**,17,**32**,33,1000} × `adlen` ∈ {0,1,15,**16**,17,31,**32**,33} | [ ] |\n303:| 178 | `crypto_aead_aegis256_encrypt_detached` / `_decrypt_detached` | same cross-product; `m == NULL` path | [ ] |\n304:| 179 | `_crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation` / `_aegis256_...` | selects the `*_soft` impl in this build | [ ] |\n305:| 180 | AEGIS `*_keygen` + all constant getters | `_keybytes` 16/32, `_npubbytes` 16/32, `_abytes` 32, `_nsecbytes` 0 | [ ] |\n306:| 181 | `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_is_available` + all 9 stubs | **0** / -1+ENOSYS for every entry point (see ERRORS 106–115); `_statebytes` still returns a 16-aligned size | [ ] |\n312:| 182 | `crypto_secretbox_easy` / `_open_easy` | `mlen` ∈ {0,1,31,**32**,33,64,1000} (block0 holds `min(mlen,32)` bytes after 32 zeros) | [ ] |\n313:| 183 | `crypto_secretbox_detached` / `_open_detached` | same `mlen` set, DISJOINT buffers | [ ] |\n314:| 184 | `crypto_secretbox_detached` / `_open_detached` | **overlap axis**: in-place `c == m`; partially overlapping FORWARD; partially overlapping BACKWARD (explicit `uintptr_t` detection + `memmove`) — 4 distinct paths | [ ] |\n315:| 185 | `crypto_secretbox_detached` | `mlen` = 131072 / 131073 (`STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK`, 64-bit `ic`) | [ ] |\n316:| 186 | `crypto_secretbox` / `_open` (deprecated NaCl, requires 32 leading zeros in `m`, writes 16 leading zeros in `c`) | `mlen` ∈ {32,33,64,96,1000} | [ ] |\n317:| 187 | `crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305` / `_open` (primitive level) | same as row 186 | [ ] |\n318:| 188 | `crypto_secretbox_open_detached` with `m == NULL` | verify-only mode | [ ] |\n319:| 189 | `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_easy` / `_open_easy` | `mlen` set of row 182; `_detached` calls `chacha20_xor` over exactly `mlen0+32`, then ONE `xor_ic(1)`; poly1305 over the full ct (no chunking) | [ ] |\n320:| 190 | `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_detached` / `_open_detached` | disjoint + all 3 overlap shapes; `m == NULL` | [ ] |\n321:| 191 | `crypto_secretbox*_keygen` + `_keybytes`/`_noncebytes`/`_macbytes`/`_zerobytes`/`_boxzerobytes`/`_messagebytes_max`/`_primitive` | **[RNG]** + constants (`\"xsalsa20poly1305\"`) | [ ] |\n327:| 192 | `_init_push` / `_push` / `_init_pull` / `_pull` | TAG_MESSAGE (0x00) only; `mlen` ∈ {0 (out = 17 bytes),1,15,16,**48** (makes `(0x10-64+mlen)&0xf == 0`),63,64,65} × `adlen` ∈ {0,1,15,16,17} | [ ] |\n328:| 193 | same | TAG_PUSH (0x01) — bit 0x02 clear ⇒ NO rekey | [ ] |\n329:| 194 | same | TAG_REKEY (0x02) — triggers an automatic rekey | [ ] |\n330:| 195 | same | TAG_FINAL (0x03 = PUSH\\|REKEY) — also rekeys | [ ] |\n331:| 196 | same | ARBITRARY tag bytes {0x04, 0x42, 0x7f, 0xff}: accepted; any with bit 0x02 set rekeys | [ ] |\n332:| 197 | `_rekey` | explicit symmetric rekey mid-stream on both sides | [ ] |\n333:| 198 | multi-message sequence | 8-message stream mixing all 4 tags; MAC-chaining (`STATE_INONCE ^= tag[0..8)`) makes ordering part of the state | [ ] |\n334:| 199 | poly1305-layout quirk | the ciphertext pad is `(0x10 - 64 + mlen) & 0xf` (the source documents this as a deviation from the intended `(0x10 - (64+mlen)) & 0xf`) — wire-format visible | [ ] |\n335:| 200 | `_pull` out-params | `mlen_p == NULL` and/or `tag_p == NULL` | [ ] |\n336:| 201 | `_keygen` + `_statebytes`/`_abytes`(17)/`_headerbytes`(24)/`_keybytes`/`_messagebytes_max`/`_tag_message`/`_tag_push`/`_tag_rekey`/`_tag_final` | **[RNG]** + constants | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QjgHYweQnvDsXQS6Cy8mZK","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"a6979609-b4b1-4f2c-b973-884007838ad9","timestamp":"2026-08-14T17:38:56.401Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write AEAD/secretbox tests"}
