egis128l.rs`/`aes256gcm.rs` are byte-identical to their originals (their mtimes only moved because the mutation harness restored them via `cp`).\n\n## (d) Rows deliberately not driven on one axis\n- **CONFIGS 174 uppercase `_IETF_*` aliases**: they are preprocessor `#define`s in the public headers, not exported symbols. Covered by asserting `dlsym` fails for all 7 of them in *both* libraries (and the lowercase getters return the documented values). Same treatment for `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_keygen`, which does not exist in 1.0.23.\n- **The `mlen == MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` (no-misuse) side of ERRORS 84/92/116/122**: that bound is `2^64-17`, so the callee must compute `c + (2^64-17)` — a byte offset beyond `isize::MAX`, which a debug-profile Rust build rejects with its own `ptr::add` precondition abort (indistinguishable from SIGABRT), and which is UB in the C too and only reachable with a 16-exabyte buffer. Pinned instead by the misuse side (3 values each) plus the exact `messagebytes_max()` value. Every bound that *is* numerically representable gets both sides: ERRORS 88 (ietf, `64·(2³²−1)`), 96/101 (aegis, `2⁶¹−1`), 97/102, 125, 127 — each with a `mprotect(PROT_NONE)` guard page so the over-run faults deterministically.\n\n## Mutation checks (10 run, 10 caught)\n| # | mutation | caught by |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | ietf ciphertext pad → `0` | r167, r168, r169, r172 |\n| M2 | secretstream pad → the \"intended\" `(0x10-(64+mlen))&0xf` | r199, r192, r198 |\n| M3 | delete the `uintptr_t` overlap detection + `memmove` in `crypto_secretbox_detached` | r184 |\n| M4 | `aes256gcm_is_available()` → 1 | r181, e106_e115 |\n| M5 | drop `errno = ENOSYS` in `_beforenm` | r181, e106_e115 |\n| M6 | drop `memset(m,0,mlen)` on MAC failure in `cp_decrypt_detached` | e86_e87, r164, r165, r173 |\n| M7 | write `*maclen_p` *after* the aegis128l bound check | e97 |\n| M8 | advance the secretstream state on a forged `_pull` | e128, r197, r198 |\n| M9 | revert real fix #2 (`xsalsa20poly1305_messagebytes_max`) | r191 |\n| M10 | xchacha ietf `ad` pad → `0` | r170, r171, r172 |\n\nAll sources restored and re-verified identical (`diff -q`) after the mutation run."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: af64d6fbc811b2216 (use SendMessage with to: 'af64d6fbc811b2216', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 314184\ntool_uses: 86\nduration_ms: 2235898</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"1afdc9de-cd42-4f30-8e9f-e2596b4a0a44","timestamp":"2026-08-14T18:16:02.427Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust differential verification of libsodium 1.0.23.\n\nREPO: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nYOUR FILE (create it, nothing else): tests/t07_aead.rs\n\n## HARD RULES\n- Do NOT modify: `c_src/**` (the C is ground truth), `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, `run_difftests.sh`, or any other `tests/t*.rs`.\n- You MAY read anything. You MAY edit files under `src/` ONLY to fix a genuine Rust translation bug proven by a failing differential test.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — every call goes through `dlsym` on BOTH shared libraries via the harness.\n- NEVER weaken/skip an assertion. The C is ALWAYS correct. If C and Rust disagree, the RUST is wrong.\n\n## BUILD (critical)\n`cargo test` does NOT rebuild the cdylib for integration tests. ALWAYS:\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/translated_rust\nulimit -c 0\ncargo build && timeout 600 cargo test --test t07_aead 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\n\n## THE HARNESS (tests/common/mod.rs — READ IT FIRST)\n```rust\nmod common; use common::*;\ninit_both();\nlet (c, r) = fnpair!(\"symbol_name\", unsafe extern \"C\" fn(A,B)->R);\nassert_eq_bytes(\"what\", &c_out, &r_out);\nRng::new(SEED); pub const LENS: &[usize]; pub fn patterns(n, &mut rng) -> Vec<Vec<u8>>\nforked(|| -> i64 { ... }) -> Outcome; Outcome::Signaled(SIGABRT); assert_same_fatal(..)\ninstall_det_rng(bool); reset_det_rng();\nlibs(); sym::<T>(&libs().c, \"name\")\n```\n**Fork hygiene**: resolve symbols and allocate buffers in the PARENT; the child closure only calls a pre-resolved fn pointer. `setrlimit(RLIMIT_CORE,0)` in fork-heavy tests.\n**Parallelism**: tests are parallel threads over one pair of `.so`s; guard `install_det_rng` users with a file-local `Mutex` and restore the default impl after.\n\n## WHAT TO COVER\nRead `CONFIGS.md` rows **164–201** and `ERRORS.md` rows **84–130** — they are your specification.\n\n**AEADs** (CONFIGS 164–181, ERRORS 84–115):\n- `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_{encrypt,decrypt,encrypt_detached,decrypt_detached,keygen}` + all constant getters (8-byte nonce, **pre-IETF** poly1305 layout: NO 16-byte padding; adlen and mlen appended as two interleaved STORE64_LE lengths)\n- `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_ietf_*` (12-byte nonce, **RFC 8439** layout with `_pad0` of `((0x10-len)&0xf)`), incl. the uppercase `crypto_aead_chacha20poly1305_IETF_*` constant aliases\n- `crypto_aead_xchacha20poly1305_ietf_*` (24-byte nonce; HChacha20 sub-key; `npub2 = 4 zero bytes || npub[16..24)`)\n- `crypto_aead_aegis128l_*` (RATE **32**, ABYTES 32, KEY 16, NPUB 16) and `crypto_aead_aegis256_*` (RATE **16**, ABYTES 32, KEY 32, NPUB 32), plus `_crypto_aead_aegis128l_pick_best_implementation` / `_aegis256_...`\n- `crypto_aead_aes256gcm_*`: in THIS build (no HAVE_TMMINTRIN_H/HAVE_WMMINTRIN_H/HAVE_ARMCRYPTO) every entry point is an **ENOSYS stub**: `_is_available()` returns **0** and all 9 functions return **-1** with `errno=ENOSYS`. ERRORS rows 106–115. Assert BOTH libs agree, including errno, for all of `_encrypt`, `_encrypt_detached`, `_decrypt`, `_decrypt_detached`, `_beforenm`, `_encrypt_afternm`, `_encrypt_detached_afternm`, `_decrypt_afternm`, `_decrypt_detached_afternm`. Also compare `_statebytes` and all constant getters.\n\n**secretbox** (CONFIGS 182–191, ERRORS 116–124):\n`crypto_secretbox_{easy,open_easy,detached,open_detached,keygen}`, the deprecated `crypto_secretbox` / `crypto_secretbox_open` (NaCl padded, needs 32 leading zero bytes in `m`, writes 16 leading zeros in `c`, requires len >= 32), `crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305` / `_open` + its getters, and the whole `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_*` set.\n**The overlap axis is mandatory** (CONFIGS 184/190): `crypto_secretbox_detached` / `_open_detached` do explicit `uintptr_t` partial-overlap detection then `memmove`. Test 4 distinct shapes: fully disjoint; in-place `c == m`; partially overlapping FORWARD; partially overlapping BACKWARD. Use one big buffer and take overlapping subslices via raw pointers.\n`mlen0 = min(mlen, 32)` is the first-block axis: sweep `mlen` ∈ {0,1,31,32,33,64,131072,131073}. 131072 is `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK`.\n\n**secretstream** (CONFIGS 192–201, ERRORS 125–130):\n`crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_{init_push,push,init_pull,pull,rekey,keygen,statebytes,abytes,headerbytes,keybytes,messagebytes_max,tag_message,tag_push,tag_rekey,tag_final}`.\n- TAG axis: MESSAGE 0x00, PUSH 0x01, REKEY 0x02, FINAL 0x03. Only bit **0x02** triggers the automatic rekey. **Arbitrary** tag bytes {0x04,0x42,0x7f,0xff} are ACCEPTED (ERRORS 130) and any with bit 0x02 set rekeys.\n- `_init_pull` accepts ANY 24-byte header with no validation (ERRORS 129); a wrong header only shows up as a MAC failure on the first `_pull`.\n- ERRORS 128: on a forged MAC, `_pull` returns -1, leaves `*mlen_p` 0 and `*tag_p` 0xff, and **does NOT advance the state**. Assert the state buffer is unchanged and that a subsequent correct `_pull` still works.\n- CONFIGS 199 is a deliberate C quirk: the ciphertext poly1305 pad is `(0x10 - 64 + mlen) & 0xf` (the source comments that the intended form was `(0x10 - (64+mlen)) & 0xf`). It is wire-format visible; `mlen = 48` makes it 0. Sweep `mlen` ∈ {0,1,15,16,48,63,64,65}.\n- Run a multi-message sequence (≥8 messages mixing all 4 tags) and compare every ciphertext and the full state after each step. MAC-chaining (`STATE_INONCE ^= tag[0..8)`) makes ordering part of the state.\n\nC sources: `c_src/libsodium/crypto_aead/**`, `crypto_secretbox/**`, `crypto_secretstream/**`. Headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`. READ them for exact signatures.\n\n### Requirements\n1. **Every** CONFIGS row 164–201 gets a `#[test]` (or clearly-named section) driving ≥64 randomized inputs.\n2. **Every** ERRORS row 84–130 gets a C-vs-Rust assertion on the return value AND the full output buffer AND out-params AND errno where applicable (abort rows via `forked` + `assert_same_fatal`, asserting the outcome really is `Signaled(SIGABRT)`).\n3. `ad == NULL` with `adlen == 0`; `nsec != NULL` (all `*_NSECBYTES == 0`); `*clen_p`/`*maclen_p`/`*mlen_p`/`*outlen_p`/`*tag_p` = NULL (CONFIGS 172, 200).\n4. `*_decrypt_detached` / `*_open_detached` with `m == NULL` — verify-only mode, a DISTINCT code path (CONFIGS 173, 188, 190).\n5. On MAC failure with `m != NULL` the C zeroes the plaintext buffer (`memset(m,0,clen)`); with `m == NULL` it does not. Assert the full buffer.\n6. Prefill every output buffer with 0xAA plus a trailing guard; compare the FULL buffer and assert the guard is intact.\n7. The 131072/131073 chunk-boundary rows matter (they exercise the `ic` carry across `STREAM_POLY1305_CHUNK`); allocate those buffers once and reuse.\n8. Opaque secretstream state: allocate via `crypto_secretstream_xchacha20poly1305_statebytes()`, oversized and 0xAA-prefilled, and compare the WHOLE state buffer between libs after every operation.\n\n## ON DIVERGENCE\n1. Print exact inputs (key, nonce, ad, mlen, tag) and the first differing byte offset.\n2. Rust sources: `src/aead/{chacha20poly1305,xchacha20poly1305,aegis128l,aegis256,aes256gcm,secretbox,secretstream,softaes}.rs`.\n3. Fix the Rust to match the C EXACTLY, including the padding quirks and the `*maclen_p`-written-before-abort behaviour.\n4. Re-run and confirm.\n5. Report EVERY `src/` edit with a one-line before/after and the proving row.\n\n## DELIVERABLE\n`tests/t07_aead.rs` compiling and PASSING. Report: (a) test count, (b) CONFIGS/ERRORS rows → test fn mapping, (c) every `src/` fix with the proving row, (d) any row not covered and precisely why. Also run ≥5 mutation checks and report them.","agentId":"af64d6fbc811b2216","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Final verification complete.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n`tests/t07_aead.rs` (4279 lines) — **73 `#[test]`s, all passing**. The whole suite still passes: `./run_difftests.sh` → 9/9 targets OK, symbol parity 890/890.\n\n## (a) Test count\n73 tests in `t07_aead`; every call routed through `dlsym` on both `.so`s (`fnpair!`/`sym`), no direct Rust calls.\n\n## (b) Row → test mapping\n**CONFIGS 164–201** (all 38 rows, each ≥64 randomized inputs, self-asserted with `assert!(iters >= 64)`):\n`r164_cp_encrypt_decrypt`, `r165_cp_detached`, `r166_cp_chunk_boundary`, `r167_cpi_encrypt_decrypt`, `r168_cpi_detached`, `r169_cpi_chunk_boundary`, `r170_xcpi_encrypt_decrypt`, `r171_xcpi_detached`, `r172_null_nsec_inplace_outparams`, `r173_decrypt_detached_verify_only`, `r174_chacha_keygen_and_constants`, `r175/r176_aegis128l_*`, `r177/r178_aegis256_*`, `r179_aegis_pick_best_implementation`, `r180_aegis_keygen_and_constants`, `r181_aes256gcm_stubs_and_constants`, `r182_secretbox_easy`, `r183_secretbox_detached_disjoint`, `r184_secretbox_detached_overlap`, `r185_secretbox_detached_chunk_boundary`, `r186_secretbox_nacl_padded`, `r187_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305`, `r188_secretbox_open_detached_verify_only`, `r189_secretbox_xchacha_easy`, `r190_secretbox_xchacha_detached_overlap`, `r191_secretbox_keygen_and_constants`, `r192…r195_ss_tag_{message,push,rekey,final}`, `r196_ss_arbitrary_tags`, `r197_ss_explicit_rekey`, `r198_ss_multi_message_sequence`, `r199_ss_pad_quirk`, `r200_ss_pull_null_outparams`, `r201_ss_keygen_and_constants`.\n\n**ERRORS 84–130** (all 47 rows): `e84`, `e85`, `e86_e87`, `e88`, `e89`, `e90_e91`, `e92`, `e93`, `e94_e95`, `e96`, `e97`, `e98`, `e99`, `e100`, `e101`, `e102`, `e103`, `e104`, `e105`, `e106_e115_aes256gcm_enosys` (+ `r181`), `e116`, `e117`, `e118`, `e119`, `e120`, `e121`, `e122`, `e123`, `e124`, `e125`, `e126`, `e127`, `e128`, `e129`, `e130`.\n\nNotable mechanisms: every abort row uses `forked` + `assert_same_fatal` and asserts the outcome really is `Signaled(SIGABRT)` (vs. a `Returned(FAULT)` SIGSEGV marker for the at-the-bound no-misuse side). ERRORS 97/102/125/127 write their out-param into an `mmap(MAP_SHARED)` page so the parent can prove `*maclen_p == 32` / `*outlen_p == 0` / `*mlen_p == 0` + `*tag_p == 0xff` were written *before* the `abort()`. Row 199 additionally re-derives the push MAC from dlsym'd `chacha20_ietf`/`poly1305` primitives of *each* library with both the quirky pad (`mlen & 0xf`) and the intended pad (`(0x10-mlen) & 0xf)`, asserting the MAC matches the quirky one and *not* the intended one (16+ inputs where they differ). Row 184/190 drive all four overlap shapes through raw offset pointers in one buffer and compare the whole buffer.\n\n## (c) `src/` fixes (each proven by a failing differential test)\n1. **10 sites** — `src/aead/chacha20poly1305.rs:176,199,357,361`, `src/aead/xchacha20poly1305.rs:70,98,136,140`, `src/aead/secretstream.rs:177,262`\n   - before: `crypto_onetimeauth_poly1305_update(&mut state, _PAD0.as_ptr(), (0x10 - adlen) & 0xf);` (same for `mlen`)\n   - after: `... (0x10u64.wrapping_sub(adlen)) & 0xf);`\n   - C's `(0x10 - len) & 0xf` is unsigned wrap-around; the Rust used checked arithmetic, so **any `adlen`/`mlen` > 16 aborted the cdylib** with \"attempt to subtract with overflow\". Proving rows: **CONFIGS 167/168** (first failure in `r167_cpi_encrypt_decrypt`), also 170/171/192.\n2. **`src/aead/secretbox.rs:80`**\n   - before: `const MESSAGEBYTES_MAX: u64 = u64::MAX;`\n   - after: `const MESSAGEBYTES_MAX: u64 = u64::MAX - MACBYTES as u64;`\n   - `crypto_secretbox_xsalsa20poly1305_messagebytes_max()` returned `18446744073709551615` vs the C's `18446744073709551599` (`crypto_stream_xsalsa20_MESSAGEBYTES_MAX - MACBYTES`). Proving row: **CONFIGS 191** (`r191_secretbox_keygen_and_constants`).\n\nNo other file was modified; `aegis128l.rs`/`aes256gcm.rs` are byte-identical to their originals (their mtimes only moved because the mutation harness restored them via `cp`).\n\n## (d) Rows deliberately not driven on one axis\n- **CONFIGS 174 uppercase `_IETF_*` aliases**: they are preprocessor `#define`s in the public headers, not exported symbols. Covered by asserting `dlsym` fails for all 7 of them in *both* libraries (and the lowercase getters return the documented values). Same treatment for `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_keygen`, which does not exist in 1.0.23.\n- **The `mlen == MESSAGEBYTES_MAX` (no-misuse) side of ERRORS 84/92/116/122**: that bound is `2^64-17`, so the callee must compute `c + (2^64-17)` — a byte offset beyond `isize::MAX`, which a debug-profile Rust build rejects with its own `ptr::add` precondition abort (indistinguishable from SIGABRT), and which is UB in the C too and only reachable with a 16-exabyte buffer. Pinned instead by the misuse side (3 values each) plus the exact `messagebytes_max()` value. Every bound that *is* numerically representable gets both sides: ERRORS 88 (ietf, `64·(2³²−1)`), 96/101 (aegis, `2⁶¹−1`), 97/102, 125, 127 — each with a `mprotect(PROT_NONE)` guard page so the over-run faults deterministically.\n\n## Mutation checks (10 run, 10 caught)\n| # | mutation | caught by |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | ietf ciphertext pad → `0` | r167, r168, r169, r172 |\n| M2 | secretstream pad → the \"intended\" `(0x10-(64+mlen))&0xf` | r199, r192, r198 |\n| M3 | delete the `uintptr_t` overlap detection + `memmove` in `crypto_secretbox_detached` | r184 |\n| M4 | `aes256gcm_is_available()` → 1 | r181, e106_e115 |\n| M5 | drop `errno = ENOSYS` in `_beforenm` | r181, e106_e115 |\n| M6 | drop `memset(m,0,mlen)` on MAC failure in `cp_decrypt_detached` | e86_e87, r164, r165, r173 |\n| M7 | write `*maclen_p` *after* the aegis128l bound check | e97 |\n| M8 | advance the secretstream state on a forged `_pull` | e128, r197, r198 |\n| M9 | revert real fix #2 (`xsalsa20poly1305_messagebytes_max`) | r191 |\n| M10 | xchacha ietf `ad` pad → `0` | r170, r171, r172 |\n\nAll sources restored and re-verified identical (`diff -q`) after the mutation run."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":2235898,"totalTokens":314184,"totalToolUseCount":86,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":309187,"output_tokens":4079,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":916},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":0,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":83,"editFileCount":3,"linesAdded":406,"linesRemoved":4,"otherToolCount":0}}}
