_kem/**`, `crypto_kx/**`. Headers in `c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/`. READ them for exact signatures.\n\n### Requirements\n1. **Every** CONFIGS row 217–244 gets a `#[test]` (or clearly-named section) driving ≥64 randomized inputs where a random shape exists; assert the iteration count in-test.\n2. **Every** ERRORS row 375–391 gets a C-vs-Rust assertion on the return value AND the full output buffer AND errno where applicable.\n3. Prefill every output buffer with 0xAA plus a trailing guard; compare the FULL buffer and assert the guard is intact.\n4. Opaque HKDF states: allocate via `crypto_kdf_hkdf_sha256_statebytes()` / `_sha512_statebytes()`, oversized and 0xAA-prefilled, and compare the WHOLE state buffer between libs after `_extract_init` and each `_extract_update`.\n5. Round-trips: kem enc→dec (ss match), kx client↔server, kdf hkdf extract→expand.\n\n## ON DIVERGENCE\n1. Print exact inputs and the first differing byte offset.\n2. Rust sources: `src/kdf_kem/{kdf,kem,kx,mlkem,xof,softaes}.rs`, `src/primitives/blake2b.rs`, `src/ed25519/x25519.rs`.\n3. Fix the Rust to match the C EXACTLY. For mlkem the usual culprits are NTT/montgomery reduction constants, the 12-bit polyvec packing, and the `du`/`dv` compression rounding.\n4. Re-run and confirm.\n5. Report EVERY `src/` edit with a one-line before/after and the proving row.\n\n## DELIVERABLE\n`tests/t09_kdf_kem.rs` compiling and PASSING. Report: (a) test count, (b) CONFIGS/ERRORS rows → test fn mapping, (c) every `src/` fix with the proving row, (d) any row not covered and precisely why. Also run ≥5 mutation checks (break a Rust fn, confirm a test catches it, revert; verify the file is byte-identical afterwards) and report them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018ueHGV19L1ynWJGuKgAwD9","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051","uuid":"09f47768-7042-4c81-853d-519561851928","timestamp":"2026-08-14T18:37:35.322Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write kdf/kem/kx tests"}
