{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a5d81a2044670041b","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01LD53KYYjGG2NYjwexHvbPz","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-nOS43A-translated-rust/94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051/tasks/a5d81a2044670041b.output","summary":"Done. `tests/t11_ipcrypt_integration.rs` compiles clean and passes; **zero `src/` changes were needed** — the Rust ipcrypt/softaes translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every axis I drove.\n\n## (a) Test count\n**17 `#[test]` functions**, stable across `--test-threads=1/4/default` (5 consecutive green full runs).\n\n## (b) Row → test mapping (iteration counts asserted in-test)\n\n| Row | Test fn | Randomized inputs |\n|---|---|---|\n| CONFIGS 265 | `cfg265_ipcrypt_encrypt_decrypt` | 154 key×IP (0x00/0xff/counter/random × 0x00/0xff/v4-mapped/native-v6/random) + raw-decrypt path |\n| CONFIGS 266 | `cfg266_ipcrypt_nd` | 352 (key×tweak×IP; asserts `out[0..8)==tweak`, tweak recovered from `in[0..8)`) |\n| CONFIGS 267 | `cfg267_ipcrypt_ndx_distinct_halves` | 352 (asserts `out[0..16)==tweak`, tweak from `in[0..16)`) |\n| CONFIGS 268 | `cfg268_ipcrypt_ndx_identical_halves` | 67 degenerate `A‖A` keys |\n| CONFIGS 269 | `cfg269_ipcrypt_pfx_ipv4_mapped_vs_native` | 131 (64 v4-mapped ⇒ `out[0..10)=0`,`out[10..12)=0xffff`; 64 native-v6 twins ⇒ must *not* look v4-mapped) |\n| CONFIGS 270 | `cfg270_ipcrypt_pfx_prefix_preservation` | 88 pairs over n∈{0,1,8,32,64,96,120,127,128}, asserting shared ciphertext prefix is **exactly** n, mixing normal and degenerate keys, plus 16 v4-mapped pairs |\n| CONFIGS 271 | `cfg271_ipcrypt_all_keygens` | 256 keygen calls; also proves each keygen consumes *exactly* keybytes from `randombytes_buf` |\n| CONFIGS 272 | `cfg272_ipcrypt_getters_and_pick_best_implementation` | 12 getters = 16,16,16,8,16,24,32,16,16,32,32,16; picker idempotent ×4, outputs unchanged |\n| CONFIGS 273 | `cfg273_ip2bin_ipcrypt_bin2ip_integration` | 66 (`\"192.0.2.1\"`, `\"2001:db8::1\"` + 64 random; both deterministic and `pfx` modes; `bin2ip` return-pointer identity checked) |\n| CONFIGS 274 | `cfg274_sign_to_box_to_secretbox_pipeline` | 64 end-to-end (ed25519 keypair → sk/pk→curve25519 → box_easy/open → beforenm-derived key → secretbox) |\n| CONFIGS 275 | `cfg275_kx_to_secretstream_pipeline` | 64 (kx×2 → client/server session keys → init_push → 8 pushes MESSAGE/PUSH/REKEY/FINAL → init_pull + 8 pulls; **full 52-byte state buffer traced after every step**) |\n| CONFIGS 276 | `cfg276_kem_to_kdf_to_aead_pipeline` | 72 (64 via `_seed_keypair`/`_enc_deterministic`, 8 via RNG `keypair`/`enc`) |\n| CONFIGS 277 | `cfg277_pwhash_to_secretbox_pipeline` | 64 (argon2id13, `opslimit=1`, `memlimit=8192`, `SALTBYTES=16`; getters asserted) |\n| CONFIGS 278 | `cfg278_pre_and_post_sodium_init` | 4077-byte result blob compared 4 ways: pre-C vs pre-Rust, post-C vs post-Rust, C pre vs post, Rust pre vs post |\n| ERRORS 392 | `err392_ipcrypt_has_no_error_paths` | all 8 entry points + 4 keygens + 12 getters + picker driven in a forked child per library; both must exit 0 (never `SIGABRT`) |\n| ERRORS 393 | `err393_degenerate_identical_key_halves` (+265/268/270) | 67 ndx + 34 pfx; proves the `^0x5a` branch is *taken* via `ndx(A‖A) == ndx((A^0x5a)‖A)` and `pfx(A‖A) == pfx(A‖(A^0x5a))` **inside each library** |\n| ERRORS 394 | `err394_siphash_any_inlen_including_zero` | 492 cases; both variants return 0 at `inlen=0` (10 cases) and over the whole `LENS` sweep; `in=NULL, inlen=0` compared via `forked` |\n\nEvery output buffer is `n+16` bytes prefilled `0xAA`; the guard is asserted intact on **both** sides and the **full** buffer (payload+guard) is compared.\n\nCONFIGS 278 mechanism: every test calls a local `init_all()` that drives a `OnceLock`-guarded `capture_preinit()` **before** `init_both()`, so the pre-init snapshot is forked before `sodium_init()` can run anywhere in the process; the child writes into an `mmap(MAP_SHARED)` page. The subset is allocation-free, stack-only, RNG-free, and pre-resolved in the parent.\n\n## (c) `src/` fixes\n**None.** `src/kdf_kem/ipcrypt.rs` md5 is `01c32f9483a6012790e03ee4f8b68bc4` before and after — unchanged. The AES key schedule/round order, the `^0x5a` re-derivation, the `pfx` bit axis and the 96-vs-0 prefix start all already match the C exactly.\n\nOne non-src finding worth recording: **`argon2_hash()` begins with `randombytes_buf(hash, hashlen)`**, so `crypto_pwhash` *consumes* from the process-global RNG stream even though its result is deterministic. That silently desynchronised the deterministic-RNG rows (271/274/275) when run in parallel; CONFIGS 277 now holds the same file-local `RNG_LOCK`.\n\n## (d) Rows not covered\nNone — 265–278 and 392–394 are all covered.\n\n## Mutation checks (11; all caught, all reverted byte-identically)\nSeven in `src/kdf_kem/ipcrypt.rs` (md5 verified equal after each revert):\n\n| # | Mutation | Caught by |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | `pfx_pad_prefix` sentinel `0x01`→`0x02` | 269, 270, 273 |\n| M2 | `diff[i] = k[i] ^ 0x5a` → `^ 0x5b` (ndx) | 268, 393, 278 |\n| M3 | `prefix_start = 96` → `0` (both pfx fns) | 269, 270, 273, 278 |\n| M4 | nd middle-round tweak XOR dropped | 266, 278 |\n| M5 | XEX final-round tweak XOR dropped | 267, 268, 393, 278 |\n| M6 | `crypto_ipcrypt_nd_outputbytes` 24→25 | 272, 278 |\n| M7 | `pfx_get_bit` byte index `15-b/8`→`b/8` | 269, 270, 273, 278 |\n\nFour on the pipeline wiring in my own test file (Rust side fed a shifted iteration index), proving the traces compare real end-to-end data: P274 caught at `box_ct`, P275 at `push[0].clen`, P276 at `kem.seed`, P277 at `pwhash.passwd`. Test-file md5 `933bf0112067a3bd14a6f9a11523714f` unchanged.\n\n## Caveat for the caller\nOther agents are editing `src/` concurrently (`kdf_kem/{mlkem,kem,kdf,kx}.rs`, `pwhash/scrypt.rs`). I observed two transient non-my-fault failure modes: the harness `STALE Rust .so` guard firing (all 17 fail in 0.01 s — fix: `cargo build`), and one transient `kem.ct` divergence in CONFIGS 276 that vanished once their mlkem edit was rebuilt. Always `cargo build` immediately before `cargo test`.","usage":{"total_tokens":233046,"tool_uses":80,"duration_ms":2167122},"uuid":"0ec6de23-b3b5-4b5c-a918-9d01673d728a","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051"}
