e `pfx` bit axis and the 96-vs-0 prefix start all already match the C exactly.\n\nOne non-src finding worth recording: **`argon2_hash()` begins with `randombytes_buf(hash, hashlen)`**, so `crypto_pwhash` *consumes* from the process-global RNG stream even though its result is deterministic. That silently desynchronised the deterministic-RNG rows (271/274/275) when run in parallel; CONFIGS 277 now holds the same file-local `RNG_LOCK`.\n\n## (d) Rows not covered\nNone — 265–278 and 392–394 are all covered.\n\n## Mutation checks (11; all caught, all reverted byte-identically)\nSeven in `src/kdf_kem/ipcrypt.rs` (md5 verified equal after each revert):\n\n| # | Mutation | Caught by |\n|---|---|---|\n| M1 | `pfx_pad_prefix` sentinel `0x01`→`0x02` | 269, 270, 273 |\n| M2 | `diff[i] = k[i] ^ 0x5a` → `^ 0x5b` (ndx) | 268, 393, 278 |\n| M3 | `prefix_start = 96` → `0` (both pfx fns) | 269, 270, 273, 278 |\n| M4 | nd middle-round tweak XOR dropped | 266, 278 |\n| M5 | XEX final-round tweak XOR dropped | 267, 268, 393, 278 |\n| M6 | `crypto_ipcrypt_nd_outputbytes` 24→25 | 272, 278 |\n| M7 | `pfx_get_bit` byte index `15-b/8`→`b/8` | 269, 270, 273, 278 |\n\nFour on the pipeline wiring in my own test file (Rust side fed a shifted iteration index), proving the traces compare real end-to-end data: P274 caught at `box_ct`, P275 at `push[0].clen`, P276 at `kem.seed`, P277 at `pwhash.passwd`. Test-file md5 `933bf0112067a3bd14a6f9a11523714f` unchanged.\n\n## Caveat for the caller\nOther agents are editing `src/` concurrently (`kdf_kem/{mlkem,kem,kdf,kx}.rs`, `pwhash/scrypt.rs`). I observed two transient non-my-fault failure modes: the harness `STALE Rust .so` guard firing (all 17 fail in 0.01 s — fix: `cargo build`), and one transient `kem.ct` divergence in CONFIGS 276 that vanished once their mlkem edit was rebuilt. Always `cargo build` immediately before `cargo test`."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":2167123,"totalTokens":236562,"totalToolUseCount