{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a9b9bff7e0e87f30b","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_018ueHGV19L1ynWJGuKgAwD9","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-nOS43A/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-nOS43A-translated-rust/94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051/tasks/a9b9bff7e0e87f30b.output","summary":"Done. `tests/t09_kdf_kem.rs` compiles and passes: **48 tests, 0 failures**, ~3 s.\n\n## (a) Test count\n48 `#[test]` functions covering CONFIGS 217–244 and ERRORS 375–391. No `src/` changes were needed — the Rust translation of `crypto_kdf`, `crypto_kem` and `crypto_kx` matched the C byte-for-byte on every input probed.\n\n## (b) Row → test mapping\n\n**CONFIGS**\n| Row | Test |\n|---|---|\n| 217 | `cfg217_kdf_blake2b_derive_from_key` (175 iters), `cfg217_kdf_blake2b_salt_personal_layout` (200) |\n| 218 | `cfg218_kdf_derive_from_key_dispatch` (200), `cfg218_kdf_constant_getters`, `cfg218_kdf_keygen_rng` (70) |\n| 219 | `cfg219_hkdf_sha256_extract_oneshot` (96) |\n| 220 | `cfg220_hkdf_sha256_extract_streaming` (~120) |\n| 221 | `cfg221_hkdf_sha256_expand` (132) |\n| 222 | `cfg222_hkdf_sha512_extract_oneshot` (96) |\n| 223 | `cfg223_hkdf_sha512_extract_streaming` (~120) |\n| 224 | `cfg224_hkdf_sha512_expand` (132) |\n| 225 | `cfg225_hkdf_keygen_rng` (80), `cfg225_hkdf_constant_getters` |\n| — | `hkdf_extract_expand_roundtrip` (80) — requirement 5 |\n| 226 | `cfg226_mlkem768_seed_keypair` (74) |\n| 227 | `cfg227_mlkem768_keypair_rng` (70) |\n| 228 | `cfg228_mlkem768_enc_deterministic` (81) |\n| 229 | `cfg229_mlkem768_enc_rng` (72) |\n| 230 | `cfg230_mlkem768_dec_valid` (72) |\n| 231 | `cfg231_e382_mlkem768_dec_tampered` (384) |\n| 232 | `cfg232_mlkem768_rej_uniform_seed_sweep` (400 keypair + 400 enc) |\n| 233 | `cfg233_xwing_seed_keypair` (73) |\n| 234 | `cfg234_xwing_keypair_rng` (70) |\n| 235 | `cfg235_xwing_enc_deterministic` (81) |\n| 236 | `cfg236_xwing_enc_dec_roundtrip` (70) |\n| 237 | `cfg237_kem_dispatch` (70), `cfg237_cfg238_kem_constant_getters` |\n| 238 | `cfg237_cfg238_kem_constant_getters` |\n| 239 | `cfg239_kx_seed_keypair` (73) |\n| 240 | `cfg240_kx_keypair_rng` (70) |\n| 241 | `cfg241_kx_full_handshake` (70) |\n| 242 | `cfg242_kx_client_session_keys_null_shapes` (70) |\n| 243 | `cfg243_kx_server_session_keys_null_shapes` (70) |\n| 244 | `cfg244_kx_constant_getters` |\n\n**ERRORS** — every row asserts return value + full output buffer + errno where applicable:\n375/376 → `e375_e376_kdf_blake2b_subkey_len_range`; 377 → `e377_kdf_derive_from_key_subkey_len_range` + `e375_e377_kdf_subkey_len_extreme_forked`; 378 → `e378_hkdf_sha256_expand_out_len_too_large`; 379 → `e379_hkdf_sha512_expand_out_len_too_large`; 380 → `e380_mlkem768_enc_deterministic_noncanonical_pk`; 381 → `e381_mlkem768_enc_noncanonical_pk`; 382 → `cfg231_e382_mlkem768_dec_tampered`; 383 → `e383_...noncanonical_mlkem_pk`; 384 → `e384_...low_order_x25519_pk`; 385 → `e385_xwing_enc_rng_sub_failures`; 386 → `e386_xwing_dec_low_order_ct`; 387 → `e387_kem_enc_dec_dispatch_propagates`; 388/390 → `e388_e390_kx_both_outputs_null_misuse` (forked, SIGABRT in both); 389 → `e389_kx_client_low_order_server_pk`; 391 → `e391_kx_server_low_order_client_pk`.\n\nBeyond byte-equality, structural identities are re-derived through *both* libraries: KDF salt=`LE64(subkey_id)‖0⁸` / personal=`ctx‖0⁸`; ML-KEM `sk = skpv‖pk‖SHA3-256(pk)‖z`, `pk[1152..] = SHA3-512(seed‖0x03)[0..32]` (the `K=3` byte), `ss = SHA3-512(m‖SHA3-256(pk))[0..32]`, implicit rejection `= SHAKE256(z‖ct)`; X-Wing `SHAKE256(seed,32)→96` split and the full combiner incl. label; kx `sk = BLAKE2b-32(seed)` and `keys = BLAKE2b-64(q‖cpk‖spk)`.\n\n## (c) `src/` fixes\n**None.** No divergence was found, so no `src/` edit was justified. All four files are byte-identical to their pre-existing state (verified by sha256 after every mutation revert).\n\n## (d) Rows not fully covered\n- **CONFIGS 232** — the `rej_uniform` refill arm cannot be observed directly through the public ABI. Covered statistically: 3 SHAKE-128 blocks give 336 candidates at a 3329/4096 acceptance rate, so ≈0.9 % of polynomials and ≈8 % of 9-polynomial matrices need the refill; 400 independent seeds are swept for `transposed=0` (keypair) and 400 for `transposed=1` (enc), so the arm fires ~30 times per direction. Rationale is in the test's doc comment.\n- Everything else is fully covered. Getter-only rows (218/225/237/238/244) have no randomized shape, so they assert exact header constants instead of an iteration count.\n\n## (e) Mutation checks (9 run, all reverted; src byte-identical afterwards)\n| # | Mutation | Caught by |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `montgomery_reduce` 62209→62210 (`mlkem.rs`) | 19 tests incl. `cfg226`, `cfg228`, `cfg231` |\n| 2 | `poly_compress_du` rounding `+Q/2` → `+Q/2+1` | 10 tests incl. `cfg228`, `cfg235`, `e380` |\n| 3 | `mlkem768_dec` returns -1 on `fail_mask != 0` | `cfg231_e382` (C=0 vs rust=-1), `cfg236`, `e386` |\n| 4 | `subkey_id` stored big-endian instead of LE | `cfg217`, `cfg217_..._layout`, `cfg218`, both `e375/376/377` |\n| 5 | HKDF-256 bound `out_len > MAX` → `>=` | `cfg221`, `e378` |\n| 6 | kx client `rx`/`tx` write order swapped | `cfg241`, `cfg242`, `e389` |\n| 7 | X-Wing combiner label last byte 0x5c→0x5d | 6 tests incl. `cfg235`, `cfg236`, `e387` |\n| 8 | `hkdf_sha256_statebytes()` returns 200 | `cfg220` (ABI check: C=208 vs rust=200), `cfg225` |\n| 9 | sha512 `extract_init` truncates `salt_len` to ≤32 | `cfg223` — fails on **state after `_extract_init`**, first differing byte 0; also `cfg222` |\n\nTwo further mutations were tried and correctly produced **no** failure because they are provably unobservable, not because of test weakness: (i) dropping the `sodium_memzero` in `hkdf_sha256_extract_final` — the C's `crypto_hash_sha256_final` already zeroes the whole state, so the wrapper's memzero is redundant; (ii) swapping the `ictx`/`octx` fields of the Rust `HmacSha256State` — only `size_of` and the address of the single `st` field are ever used, so field order is not part of the ABI.\n\nNote: a parallel agent is concurrently editing `src/kdf_kem/ipcrypt.rs` (it briefly broke the shared build with an undefined `tweak_block` at `ipcrypt.rs:47`/`:125`; it recovered on its own). That file is outside my scope and I did not touch it.","usage":{"total_tokens":243503,"tool_uses":94,"duration_ms":2305412},"uuid":"3959b09a-00a0-4df9-a6d4-9f30af07fee5","session_id":"94902601-9803-4a17-b8b6-a77154607051"}
